ady use, or use a cloud provider with your\nconsent. You can also go without: in setup, choose **Set up later**, or\n**Choose advanced options → No AI for now**."},"16":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-14","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Needs an AI model"},"17":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-15","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Works without one"},"18":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-16","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"The day's running notes and entry (**Day Summary**)"},"19":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-17","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Screen history, Activity only, Computer History"},"20":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-18","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"**Decisions** and **Commitments** on a day page"},"21":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-19","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Text recognition and search, including search by meaning, which uses its own on-device search model"},"22":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-20","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"The meeting **Summary**, the **As we go** digest, live Ask, templates"},"23":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-21","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Meeting recording, transcription and speaker labels"},"24":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-22","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Written answers in &#x2A;*Ask your memory…**, &#x2A;*Ask this day…**, &#x2A;*Ask this meeting…** and the **Ask** tab of Memory (also called Second Brain)"},"25":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-23","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Search results as cards with their sources"},"26":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-24","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"The Reflection and **Who you are** in Memory, the explanation of a connection"},"27":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-25","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Memory's counts, Insights, Connections and the graph"},"28":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-26","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Meeting to-dos in Today's focus"},"29":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-27","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-uses-ai","content":"Open loops and cooling threads, related moments, email and event drafts, Export"},"30":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-28","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"Pick one in **Settings** (⌘,) → **AI & summaries** → **AI connection** → **AI option**."},"31":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-29","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"Option"},"32":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-30","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"Runs where"},"33":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-31","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"Key"},"34":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-32","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**Everpaper Native (macOS 27)**"},"35":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-33","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"inside Everpaper"},"36":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-34","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"none"},"37":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-35","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**oMLX**"},"38":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-36","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"on this Mac; Everpaper can install it for you"},"39":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-37","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"optional"},"40":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-38","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**LM Studio**, **Ollama**, **Nativ**"},"41":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-39","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"your own app on this Mac"},"42":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-40","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"optional (Ollama: none)"},"43":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-41","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**OpenAI-Compatible**"},"44":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-42","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"any endpoint you enter"},"45":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-43","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"optional"},"46":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-44","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**Anthropic**, **OpenAI**, **Google Gemini**, **OpenRouter**"},"47":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-45","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"cloud"},"48":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-46","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"required"},"49":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-47","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**None**"},"50":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-48","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"—"},"51":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-49","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"—"},"52":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-50","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#your-options","content":"**Nativ** is a separate local server app. It is not Everpaper Native. Apple\nIntelligence is not an option in this beta. On macOS 15 and 26, Everpaper\nNative doesn't appear in the list."},"53":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-51","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#everpaper-native-macos-27","content":"On macOS 27, Everpaper can run a model inside the app, with no server to\ninstall. Macs with 16 GB of memory or more get **Gemma 4 E4B**: about a 5.9 GB\ndownload, about 8.5 GB on disk (some tools show 7.9 GB), and about 16 GB of\nfree space needed while it installs. Macs with less get **Qwen3 4B**: about\n2 GB to download, 2.3 GB on disk and about 5.5 GB free while it installs."},"54":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-52","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#everpaper-native-macos-27","content":"Setup checks the space first and verifies the download. If the connection\ndrops for a moment, the download carries on where it stopped. Everpaper\nswitches over only after the model has answered a first request, and your\ncurrent AI keeps working until then. The first request after the engine starts\ncan take up to about 30 seconds."},"55":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-53","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#everpaper-native-macos-27","content":"Between uses the engine stays loaded until your next journal review is due\n(about 13 minutes with the default 10-minute review), so each review finds it\nready. On Macs with 16 GB of memory or less, or when memory is tight, it\ncloses about a minute after use. While you record a meeting it steps aside\nright away, unless the As we go digest is running on it. Stopping an answer\ndoesn't restart it."},"56":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-54","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#everpaper-native-macos-27","content":"If you already use Everpaper Native with Qwen on a Mac with 16 GB or more, a\none-time card, **Gemma 4 E4B writes a better journal**, offers the switch. The\nsame offer stays in Settings as **Get Gemma 4 E4B**. Qwen stays on your Mac\nuntil you choose **Remove Qwen3 4B** on the card, or **Remove** in Settings."},"57":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-55","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"In setup's **Private summaries** step, Everpaper recommends one option for this\nMac and downloads nothing until you press **Prepare on this Mac**. (After\nsetup, the search model can still set itself up in the background; see\nSearch by meaning.) It decides in this order:"},"58":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-56","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**An AI setup you already have is kept**: Everpaper Native, Managed oMLX,\nLM Studio or Ollama."},"59":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-57","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**LM Studio or Ollama, if it's running with a chat model.** Everpaper uses\nit as it is and installs nothing for it."},"60":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-58","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**Everpaper Native with Gemma 4 E4B**, on macOS 27 with 16 GB of memory or\nmore."},"61":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-59","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**Your local app, once it's ready.** If LM Studio is installed but not\nrunning, or LM Studio or Ollama is running without a chat model, setup says\nso. Start it or load a model, then press **Rescan**."},"62":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-60","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**Otherwise, Managed oMLX**: Gemma 4 E4B on Macs with 24 GB or more,\nLFM2.5 2.6B below that. On macOS 27 Macs under 16 GB, Everpaper Native with\nQwen3 4B instead."},"63":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-61","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**Prepare on this Mac** also downloads the search model, and, if you chose\nmeetings, the Everyday meeting models for live captions and speaker labels.\n**Set up later** postpones the search model by a week. The Detailed meeting\nmodel isn't part of setup; add it later in **Settings → Speech** (see\nEveryday or Detailed)."},"64":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-62","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#what-setup-picks","content":"**Choose advanced options** shows every route: **Everpaper Native** (on\nmacOS 27), **Managed oMLX**, any local servers it found (with **Connect**),\n**Use my own provider** (LM Studio, Ollama, Nativ, a custom endpoint or a cloud\nprovider; finish with **Test & Use**), and **No AI for now**."},"65":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-63","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Everpaper installs the oMLX server (from GitHub) and the model you choose (from\nHugging Face), then runs them for you. In setup's advanced options, pick a\nmodel and press **Install and prepare**. The one marked **SUGGESTED** is the\nrecommendation for this Mac. The choices:"},"66":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-64","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Model"},"67":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-65","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Download"},"68":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-66","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Shown on"},"69":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-67","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Gemma 4 E4B"},"70":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-68","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"about 6.9 GB"},"71":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-69","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"24 GB of memory or more (suggested there)"},"72":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-70","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Qwen3.5 4B"},"73":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-71","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"about 4 GB"},"74":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-72","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"24 GB or more"},"75":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-73","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Qwen3.5 9B"},"76":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-74","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"about 8.2 GB"},"77":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-75","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"32 GB or more"},"78":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-76","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"LFM2.5 2.6B"},"79":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-77","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"about 1.9 GB"},"80":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-78","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"every Mac (suggested below 24 GB)"},"81":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-79","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"LFM2 1.2B"},"82":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-80","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"about 2.3 GB"},"83":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-81","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"every Mac; best for shorter meetings"},"84":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-82","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"Macs with 48 GB or more also see a few larger models marked as not yet\navailable. They can't be chosen in this beta."},"85":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-83","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#managed-omlx","content":"During a Detailed meeting on a Mac with less than 32 GB, Gemma 4 E4B steps\naside to leave room for the meeting model. While it does, the As we go digest\nis skipped, and the summary and journal wait until the meeting ends. If you\nset Gemma up yourself on a Mac with less than 24 GB, it steps aside during\nevery meeting."},"86":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-84","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#lm-studio-ollama-nativ-and-your-own-endpoint","content":"If you already run LM Studio or Ollama, Everpaper uses a chat model it already\nhas; it never downloads into another app. On Macs with 24 GB or more, the\nsuggested model is Gemma 4 E4B: `google/gemma-4-e4b` in LM Studio,\n`gemma4:e4b` in Ollama. **OpenAI-Compatible** works with any server that speaks\nthe OpenAI API: enter its base URL and model."},"87":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-85","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#llamacpp-engine-experimental","content":"**Settings → AI & summaries → AI connection → llama.cpp engine\n(experimental)** is off by default. Turned on, it runs Gemma 4 E4B on this Mac\nthrough a different engine, which is lighter on the Mac while it writes but\nslower to read long prompts. It needs a Mac with at least 16 GB of memory and\ndownloads its model (about 5.2 GB) the first time. Everpaper switches only\nafter the model has answered a first request. While it's on, **AI option**\nreads **llama.cpp engine**. Turn the switch off to go back to the AI option\nyou had before."},"88":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-86","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#when-ai-work-runs","content":"Anything you're waiting for, such as an answer you asked for, goes first.\nBackground work waits its turn. Work nobody is waiting on, such as catch-up\nwrite-ups and bringing older history up to date for search, waits for a quiet\nmoment: it holds off while another app uses the microphone, while you record a\nmeeting, while an app is in full screen, when the Mac is hot or short on\nmemory, in Low Power Mode, on battery, and while you're using the Mac. A\nlocked screen counts as a quiet moment. The running notes hold off only while\nyou record a meeting, in Low Power Mode, when the Mac is hot or very short on\nmemory, and on battery if **Reduce work on battery** is on. Work with a\ndeadline still gets done in time."},"89":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-87","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#when-ai-work-runs","content":"At launch, the Reflection and catch-up write-ups wait for the first quiet\nmoment. When Everpaper starts at login without opening a window, they wait\nuntil you open it, or for a quiet moment about 15 minutes later."},"90":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-88","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#when-ai-work-runs","content":"**Settings → General → AI work** shows whether **Background AI** is running\nor paused and why (for example **Paused: microphone in use by** and the app's\nname); Today shows the same line while work is paused. **AI use today** lists\nhow much each feature used the AI today."},"91":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-89","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"**No AI set up:** nothing is sent."},"92":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-90","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"**Everpaper Native:** runs inside the app."},"93":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-91","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"**oMLX, LM Studio, Ollama, Nativ:** private while their address is on this\nMac, which is the default. Point one at another computer and Everpaper treats\nit like a cloud provider."},"94":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-92","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"**OpenAI-Compatible:** private only while **This is a trusted, private\nendpoint** is on. It starts on for an address on this Mac and off for any\nother. Turn it on only for a server you control: a trusted endpoint receives\ntext without the cloud switch, with only secrets removed."},"95":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-93","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"**Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, OpenRouter:** nothing is sent until you\nturn on **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** (Settings → **AI &\nsummaries** → **Your memory & summaries**). It's off by default and also\nappears in Settings → **Privacy** as **Allow online journal analysis**. Until\nyou turn it on, summaries, Memory and the other AI features wait. **Share\nyour profile with cloud AI** is a separate switch beneath it."},"96":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-94","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"Secrets such as keys, tokens and card numbers are removed before any AI call.\nFor cloud providers, and endpoints you haven't marked trusted, Everpaper also\nreplaces email addresses, phone numbers and names it detects. When every\nprovider you use is private, Settings says &#x2A;Your AI uses only on-device or\ntrusted private providers — cloud AI is off.*"},"97":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-95","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#where-your-text-goes","content":"Setting up a model downloads it from Hugging Face, GitHub (oMLX) or Everpaper's\ndownload server. See Privacy for everything else."},"98":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-96","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#change-test-or-remove","content":"Open **Settings → AI & summaries → AI connection** and pick an **AI option**.\nEnter a key, address or model if asked; **Refresh list** reads the models a\nserver offers. Then press **Save** and **Test Connection**. **Clear**\ndisconnects the current AI and removes its key. An asterisk beside the section\nmeans nothing is set up or the last test failed."},"99":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-97","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#change-test-or-remove","content":"With Everpaper Native selected, the same place lists its models by name: set\none up (**Set up** or **Get**, followed by the model's name), **Cancel** a\ndownload, or **Remove** a model that's installed but not in use. To go through\nthe guided choice again, use **Settings → General → Setup & data → Run setup\nagain**."},"100":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-98","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#files-and-other-ai-apps","content":"In **Settings → AI & summaries**, under **Files you include**, choose **Add\nFolder** to let Memory's **Ask** and the Concordance answer from your\ndocuments. They're indexed on this Mac with the same on-device search model as\neverything else: **Search model** in the same place chooses\n&#x2A;*EmbeddingGemma-2 (default)** or &#x2A;*Apple (previous)**. See\nSearch by meaning."},"101":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-99","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#files-and-other-ai-apps","content":"**External embeddings provider** (advanced, optional) points file indexing at\na server you run instead: Ollama, LM Studio, oMLX or an OpenAI-compatible\nendpoint. It's separate from your chat AI, and the same rules about where text\ngoes apply to it. With none set, files use the search model."},"102":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-100","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#files-and-other-ai-apps","content":"In the same section, under **Access from other AI apps**, &#x2A;*Allow external\nagents (MCP)*&#x2A; (off by default) lets AI apps on this Mac read your people,\nfiles, links and connections, with secrets removed (names, email addresses and\nphone numbers are kept). They never get screenshots, and raw screen text needs\na second switch, &#x2A;*…including raw screen text (full-text search)**. What an\nagent reads is then handled by that app and the AI it uses, which may be a\ncloud service. **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** doesn't apply to it,\nso turn this on only for apps you trust. To connect an app, see\nCommand line."},"103":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-101","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"Gemma 4 E4B in Everpaper Native hasn't been tested on a real 16 GB Mac yet."},"104":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-102","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"The first request after the engine starts can take up to about 30 seconds.\nWhen the engine has closed to free memory, the next request waits for it to\nload again."},"105":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-103","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"The llama.cpp engine is experimental and off by default."},"106":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-104","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"Preparing the search model takes a few minutes the first time and again\nafter a macOS update; until then, search works as before. Screenshot and\nmeeting-audio search need macOS 27."},"107":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-105","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"Evening entries can condense busy days and leave out some meeting details."},"108":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-106","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"In Memory, the answer check can occasionally remove a correct detail or let\nan invented name through, so check the sources."},"109":{"id":"/ai-on-your-mac-107","page_id":"/ai-on-your-mac","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/ai-on-your-mac#known-limits-in-this-beta","content":"No new Episodes are written in this beta, so on a new install Memory's\nEpisodes tab stays empty."},"110":{"id":"/calendar","page_id":"/calendar","type":"page","content":"Calendar Auto-Start","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar"},"111":{"id":"/calendar-0","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar","content":"Let Everpaper watch your calendar to remind you before meetings or start recording for you. Everpaper only reads your calendar and never uploads it."},"112":{"id":"/calendar-1","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#connect-a-calendar","content":"Connect a calendar"},"113":{"id":"/calendar-2","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#choose-a-behavior","content":"Choose a behavior"},"114":{"id":"/calendar-3","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"Start prompt"},"115":{"id":"/calendar-4","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"Meeting eligibility"},"116":{"id":"/calendar-5","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"The countdown"},"117":{"id":"/calendar-6","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#where-upcoming-meetings-appear","content":"Where upcoming meetings appear"},"118":{"id":"/calendar-7","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#changes-apply-right-away","content":"Changes apply right away"},"119":{"id":"/calendar-8","page_id":"/calendar","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/calendar#what-everpaper-keeps-from-your-calendar","content":"What Everpaper keeps from your calendar"},"120":{"id":"/calendar-9","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar","content":"Everpaper can watch your calendar so you never miss the start of a meeting. When\nan upcoming event matches your rules, Everpaper either drops a quiet reminder or\nopens a short, cancellable countdown and starts recording for you."},"121":{"id":"/calendar-10","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar","content":"Nothing happens until you grant calendar access. The **Calendar behavior**\nsetting controls reminders and auto-start; see\nWhat Everpaper keeps from your calendar\nfor the one thing that happens whatever the setting."},"122":{"id":"/calendar-11","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#connect-a-calendar","content":"Open **Settings → Meetings** and scroll to **Calendar**, or click\n**Connect Calendar** in the **Upcoming** card on the Meetings page."},"123":{"id":"/calendar-12","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#connect-a-calendar","content":"Click **Grant Calendar Access**. macOS asks once for full calendar access,\nthe only level that lets an app read events; Everpaper only reads them."},"124":{"id":"/calendar-13","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#connect-a-calendar","content":"The rest of the calendar settings appear. Choose a **Calendar behavior**."},"125":{"id":"/calendar-14","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#connect-a-calendar","content":"Your events stay on your Mac, and Everpaper never uploads them. Everpaper keeps\nno copy of your calendar."},"126":{"id":"/calendar-15","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#connect-a-calendar","content":"macOS only asks for calendar permission once. If you decline, you can re-enable\nit later in **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Calendars**."},"127":{"id":"/calendar-16","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#choose-a-behavior","content":"Set **Calendar behavior** to one of three modes:"},"128":{"id":"/calendar-17","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#choose-a-behavior","content":"**Off**: no reminders and no countdowns. This is the default."},"129":{"id":"/calendar-18","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#choose-a-behavior","content":"**Notify before meetings**: a quiet note slips in before each meeting begins.\nNothing records on its own."},"130":{"id":"/calendar-19","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#choose-a-behavior","content":"**Start recording automatically**: Everpaper gives you five seconds to\ncancel, then starts recording."},"131":{"id":"/calendar-20","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#choose-a-behavior","content":"When you pick a mode other than Off, Everpaper asks for notification permission\nso reminders can appear. If notifications are turned off in System Settings,\nEverpaper shows a warning with a shortcut to fix it."},"132":{"id":"/calendar-21","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"Under **Start prompt**, choose when the notification arrives:"},"133":{"id":"/calendar-22","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"**When it begins**"},"134":{"id":"/calendar-23","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"**1 minute early**"},"135":{"id":"/calendar-24","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"**5 minutes early** (default)"},"136":{"id":"/calendar-25","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"**10 minutes early**"},"137":{"id":"/calendar-26","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"Each reminder fires once per meeting. If your Mac is asleep or busy at the exact\nmoment, Everpaper still catches the reminder for a short window afterward so a\nlate tick won't make you miss it."},"138":{"id":"/calendar-27","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#start-prompt","content":"The notification looks like *Weekly sync starts in 5 minutes*, with the call\nservice underneath when the event has a call link. It arrives in both\n**Notify before meetings** and **Start recording automatically**. With\n**Start recording automatically**, the countdown appears at the meeting's start\ntime, whatever you choose here."},"139":{"id":"/calendar-28","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"Not every calendar entry is a meeting. Under **Meeting eligibility**, choose how\nmuch an event needs before it counts:"},"140":{"id":"/calendar-29","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"**Events with a call link** (default): a recognized link from Zoom, Google\nMeet, Microsoft Teams, Webex, Around or Whereby, or another link that looks\nlike a call."},"141":{"id":"/calendar-30","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"**Events with guests**: at least one other person invited."},"142":{"id":"/calendar-31","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"**Every event**: every timed event."},"143":{"id":"/calendar-32","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"The stricter choices skip personal blocks and solo focus time. All-day events\nand meetings you've declined are always skipped, whatever you choose."},"144":{"id":"/calendar-33","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#meeting-eligibility","content":"If you have several calendars, expand **Calendars** to exclude specific ones: a\npersonal calendar, say, while keeping your work calendar. New calendars are\nincluded by default."},"145":{"id":"/calendar-34","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"In **Start recording automatically** mode, when a matching meeting begins\nEverpaper opens a small countdown in the top-right corner. It shows the meeting\ntitle, the service name, and the attendee count, and counts down for 5 seconds."},"146":{"id":"/calendar-35","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"Do nothing, and recording starts when the countdown ends."},"147":{"id":"/calendar-36","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"Click anywhere on the countdown, or its ✕, to cancel. That meeting won't try\nagain."},"148":{"id":"/calendar-37","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"The countdown has no keyboard shortcuts; use the mouse or trackpad."},"149":{"id":"/calendar-38","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"The countdown only appears when you're not already recording, and only for\nmeetings you've accepted or tentatively accepted (and your own blocks that have\nno invitation to answer). Meetings you haven't responded to won't auto-record,\nsince recording an unaccepted meeting would be a surprise. You can still get a\nreminder for them."},"150":{"id":"/calendar-39","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"The countdown can only open in the first 30 seconds of the meeting. If your Mac\nwas asleep then, Everpaper won't start recording late, but you'll still get the\nnotification for up to two minutes after the start. If the previous meeting is\nstill being saved, Everpaper keeps trying during those 30 seconds."},"151":{"id":"/calendar-40","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#the-countdown","content":"Calendar data never stops a recording. If a meeting runs long, Everpaper keeps\nrecording until you stop it yourself."},"152":{"id":"/calendar-41","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#where-upcoming-meetings-appear","content":"With a behavior other than Off, the **Upcoming** card on the Meetings page lists\nyour next matching meetings for the coming week, and lets you switch\n**When a meeting starts** (Off, Notify, Auto-start) and **Meeting eligibility**\nwithout opening Settings. The **Next meeting** card on Today shows the next one.\nClick **Record now** to start a recording named after it."},"153":{"id":"/calendar-42","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#changes-apply-right-away","content":"Any change you make takes effect immediately. Switch back to **Off** and\nEverpaper stops watching for upcoming meetings: no reminders, no countdowns, no\nbackground timer. Change the start prompt, the eligibility or the excluded\ncalendars and the next reminder or countdown follows the new rules. If a\ncountdown is on screen when you change a setting, it closes."},"154":{"id":"/calendar-43","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#what-everpaper-keeps-from-your-calendar","content":"Everpaper only reads your calendar. It keeps no copy and never uploads it. Once\naccess is granted, Everpaper also uses your calendar after each recording,\nwhatever the behavior: a meeting that still has its default name takes the\ntitle of the event it overlapped, and in a one-to-one call the other speaker can\nbe named from the invite (*from the calendar invite* on the **Speakers** tab).\nThose details travel with the meeting like any title or name you type, for\nexample to an AI provider you set up. To stop all of this, remove Everpaper's\naccess in **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Calendars**."},"155":{"id":"/calendar-44","page_id":"/calendar","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/calendar#what-everpaper-keeps-from-your-calendar","content":"To check which events match your rules from Terminal, see\nCommand line."},"156":{"id":"/cli","page_id":"/cli","type":"page","content":"Command line","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli"},"157":{"id":"/cli-0","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli","content":"everpaper-cli is a companion tool that shares the app's database — list and export meetings, transcribe files on-device, manage speech models, inspect Memory, connect other AI apps (MCP), and run LLM tasks from the terminal."},"158":{"id":"/cli-1","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#where-the-binary-lives","content":"Where the binary lives"},"159":{"id":"/cli-2","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#meetings","content":"Meetings"},"160":{"id":"/cli-3","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"Transcribe"},"161":{"id":"/cli-4","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#models","content":"Models"},"162":{"id":"/cli-5","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#memory-second-brain","content":"Memory (Second Brain)"},"163":{"id":"/cli-6","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#llm","content":"LLM"},"164":{"id":"/cli-7","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#everpaper-native","content":"Everpaper Native"},"165":{"id":"/cli-8","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"Connect another AI app (MCP)"},"166":{"id":"/cli-9","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"Other commands"},"167":{"id":"/cli-10","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#import","content":"Import"},"168":{"id":"/cli-11","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#json-output","content":"JSON output"},"169":{"id":"/cli-12","page_id":"/cli","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/cli#exit-codes","content":"Exit codes"},"170":{"id":"/cli-13","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli","content":"Everpaper ships with a companion command-line tool, `everpaper-cli`, that talks\nto the same database as the app. Anything you record, transcribe, or learn in\nthe app is visible from the terminal, and anything the CLI writes shows up in\nthe app. It is handy for scripting, exporting, and feeding your transcripts into\nother tools."},"171":{"id":"/cli-14","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli","content":"Most commands accept `--json` for machine-readable output (for a transcript as\nJSON, use `meetings export <id> --format json --stdout`). Progress and status\nmessages go to standard error, so the JSON on standard output stays pipeable."},"172":{"id":"/cli-15","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli","content":"By default the CLI uses the app's shared database. Pass `--database <path>` on\nmost commands to point at a different one."},"173":{"id":"/cli-16","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#where-the-binary-lives","content":"`everpaper-cli` lives inside the app at\n`/Applications/Everpaper.app/Contents/MacOS/everpaper-cli` (a `hindsight-cli`\nalias sits next to it for old scripts). To run it as a bare command, link it\nonto your `PATH`:"},"174":{"id":"/cli-17","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#where-the-binary-lives","content":"The link keeps working when you install a newer build over the old one."},"175":{"id":"/cli-18","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#meetings","content":"Work with your saved meeting recordings and their transcripts."},"176":{"id":"/cli-19","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#meetings","content":"You can refer to a meeting by its full ID, a unique ID prefix (at least four hex\ncharacters), or its exact title (letter case doesn't matter)."},"177":{"id":"/cli-20","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#meetings","content":"**Export** supports several formats with `--format`: `txt` (default),\n`markdown`, `srt`, `vtt`, and `json`. By default the file is written as\n`<title>.<ext>` in the current directory; use `--output <path>` to choose the\nname, or `--stdout` to print instead of writing a file."},"178":{"id":"/cli-21","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#meetings","content":"Each meeting also keeps **notes** and saved **results** (the output of prompts\nyou ran on it):"},"179":{"id":"/cli-22","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#meetings","content":"For `notes set` and `results add`, pass `-` instead of the text to read it from\nstandard input."},"180":{"id":"/cli-23","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#meetings","content":"Have a transcript from somewhere else? Import a WebVTT file as a meeting with\nno audio:"},"181":{"id":"/cli-24","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"Transcribe any audio or video file with the on-device speech engines. The file\nis decoded to audio and recognized locally — nothing leaves your Mac."},"182":{"id":"/cli-25","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"Key options:"},"183":{"id":"/cli-26","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"`--engine`: `app-default` (default; the **Transcription model** chosen in\nSettings → **Speech**, which is Parakeet unless you changed it), `parakeet`,\n`nemotron`, `whisper`, or `moss` (the Detailed model; about 2 GB to download\nthe first time)."},"184":{"id":"/cli-27","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"`--language`: a language hint for `nemotron` or `whisper`, e.g. `en`, `it`.\nWithout it, Whisper uses the language set in the app."},"185":{"id":"/cli-28","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"`--format`: `text` (default), `transcript` (timestamped lines), or `json`."},"186":{"id":"/cli-29","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"`--processing`: `raw` keeps the engine's text; `clean` rebuilds punctuation\nand applies your **Word corrections** (Settings → **Speech** → **Your words &\nphrases**), as the app does for meetings. The default, `app-default`, uses a\npreference older versions stored and otherwise behaves like `raw`. Pass\n`clean` to match the app. With `--diarize`, the output is speaker-labeled\ntext and this option is ignored."},"187":{"id":"/cli-30","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"`--diarize`: separate speakers and label each turn (Speaker 1, Speaker 2, …).\nWith `nemotron` it uses Nemotron's speaker labels, and with `moss` the\nmodel's own. The acoustic diarizer (used by the other engines, and as\nNemotron's fallback) is tuned with `--diar-max-distance` (default `0.775`;\nhigher merges more voices into fewer speakers), `--diar-merge-similarity`\n(default `0.85`), `--diar-min-speaker-ms` (default `2000`) and, optionally,\n`--diar-max-speakers` (no limit by default)."},"188":{"id":"/cli-31","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"`--no-save`: transcribe without adding the result to your library."},"189":{"id":"/cli-32","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#transcribe","content":"By default the result is saved to your library so it appears in the app."},"190":{"id":"/cli-33","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#models","content":"Manage the on-device speech models."},"191":{"id":"/cli-34","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#models","content":"`models download` fetches `nemotron`, `whisper` or `moss` ahead of time;\nParakeet downloads itself on first use. `models warm-up` loads an engine so the\nfirst transcription starts fast (`--engine` defaults to `nemotron`; it may\ndownload first). `models clear` deletes the speech models Everpaper downloaded\nfor transcription, including the ones it uses for meetings (Parakeet, Nemotron\nand the Detailed model). The app downloads them again when it next needs them,\nso your next meeting may start with a download."},"192":{"id":"/cli-35","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#memory-second-brain","content":"Inspect what Everpaper has learned about you (the Memory page\nin the app) and verify it against the same guard the app uses, without opening\nthe app."},"193":{"id":"/cli-36","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#memory-second-brain","content":"The output lists each belief with its salience, confidence, and evidence count,\nand reports how many would be kept versus dropped by the current guard. Add\n`--include-inactive` to also show dormant or retired beliefs."},"194":{"id":"/cli-37","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"Run language-model tasks from the terminal. Unlike the app, the CLI is\nconfigured per call — you pass the provider and key on each invocation; nothing\nis stored."},"195":{"id":"/cli-38","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"The CLI doesn't use the app's cloud AI switch. Naming a cloud provider and key\non the command line is your consent for that one call. Before anything is sent,\nsecrets such as API keys, tokens and card numbers are removed; names are not.\n`llm chat` and `prompts run` send the meeting's full transcript and notes to the\nprovider you name. Use a local provider (`ollama`, `lmstudio`, `omlx`, `nativ`)\nto keep them on your Mac."},"196":{"id":"/cli-39","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"Supported providers: `anthropic`, `openai`, `openaiCompatible`, `gemini`,\n`openrouter`, `ollama`, `lmstudio`, `omlx`, and `nativ` (the separate Nativ\nserver app). Everpaper Native isn't one of them; to test it from the terminal, use `native check`."},"197":{"id":"/cli-40","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"How the key is resolved, in order: `--api-key` (a literal — discouraged), then\n`--api-key-env` (the name of an environment variable holding the key), then the\nconventional variable for the provider (for example `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`). `ollama`, `lmstudio`,\n`omlx` and `nativ` need no key; if your LM Studio, oMLX or Nativ server uses a\ntoken, set `LM_API_TOKEN`, `OMLX_API_TOKEN` or `NATIV_API_TOKEN`."},"198":{"id":"/cli-41","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"Other useful options:"},"199":{"id":"/cli-42","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"`--model`: pick a model. Required for `openaiCompatible`, `lmstudio`, `omlx`\nand `nativ`; other providers fall back to a conservative default."},"200":{"id":"/cli-43","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"`--base-url`: an absolute `http(s)` URL for self-hosted endpoints."},"201":{"id":"/cli-44","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"`--allow-insecure-http`: permits plain `http` to a remote cloud-style\nendpoint (your key travels unencrypted)."},"202":{"id":"/cli-45","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#llm","content":"`--local`: uses the smaller context budget meant for local models."},"203":{"id":"/cli-46","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#everpaper-native","content":"On macOS 27, you can check Everpaper Native without opening\nthe app:"},"204":{"id":"/cli-47","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#everpaper-native","content":"`native check` sends one prompt through Everpaper Native and prints the model,\nthe reply, token counts and latency. `native models` lists the installed models."},"205":{"id":"/cli-48","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"Other AI apps can read from your journal through the Model Context Protocol\n(MCP). It's off until you turn it on:"},"206":{"id":"/cli-49","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"In Everpaper, turn on Settings → **AI & summaries** → **Access from other AI\napps** → &#x2A;*Allow external agents (MCP)**."},"207":{"id":"/cli-50","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"In your AI app's MCP settings, add a server that runs the command\n`/Applications/Everpaper.app/Contents/MacOS/everpaper-cli` with the\nargument `mcp`."},"208":{"id":"/cli-51","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"In apps configured with JSON, the entry usually looks like this:"},"209":{"id":"/cli-52","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"Agents get people, files, links and connections from your journal, with\nsecrets removed (names, email addresses and phone numbers are kept), and never\nscreenshots. Full-text search of your screen text needs a second switch,\n&#x2A;*…including raw screen text (full-text search)**, which appears once the first\none is on."},"210":{"id":"/cli-53","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"What an agent reads is then handled by that app and the AI it uses, which may\nbe a cloud service. **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** doesn't apply to\nit, so turn MCP on only for apps you trust."},"211":{"id":"/cli-54","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#connect-another-ai-app-mcp","content":"If your agent reports *Enable it in Everpaper → Settings → Journal*, the switch\nis at Settings → **AI & summaries** → **Access from other AI apps** → &#x2A;*Allow\nexternal agents (MCP)**."},"212":{"id":"/cli-55","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`prompts run \"Meeting Memo\" <meeting> --provider …` runs a template and saves\nthe result to the meeting (`prompts list|show|add|set|delete|restore-defaults`\nmanage them)."},"213":{"id":"/cli-56","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`calendar upcoming` lists the events your calendar rules match in the next 7\ndays."},"214":{"id":"/cli-57","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`health` checks paths, the database, models and calendar access."},"215":{"id":"/cli-58","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`vocab` manages word corrections and saved phrases."},"216":{"id":"/cli-59","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`history` lists and searches saved transcriptions."},"217":{"id":"/cli-60","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`config` reads and writes settings."},"218":{"id":"/cli-61","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#other-commands","content":"`ai-usage` shows how much each feature used the AI today: calls, prompt and\ngenerated tokens, and time. `--day YYYY-MM-DD` picks another day, `--days N`\nthe most recent N days with any use, and `--json` prints JSON."},"219":{"id":"/cli-62","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#import","content":"Bring data over from the old Hindsight app (the same import as Settings →\n**General** → **Setup & data** → &#x2A;*Import from Hindsight (legacy)**). Quit Hindsight first. Your\noriginals are never changed, and nothing imports on its own. Use\n`--legacy-root <folder>` if Hindsight's data isn't in its usual place."},"220":{"id":"/cli-63","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#import","content":"`--dry-run` shows the per-table counts (imported, skipped, unsupported) without\nwriting anything. Add `--json` for a structured report."},"221":{"id":"/cli-64","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#json-output","content":"Pass `--json` to get stable, pretty-printed JSON with sorted keys and ISO-8601\ndates. Status text is kept off standard output, so you can pipe results\nstraight into other tools:"},"222":{"id":"/cli-65","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#json-output","content":"On failure in `--json` mode, the tool prints an error envelope instead of the\nnormal payload:"},"223":{"id":"/cli-66","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#json-output","content":"Parsing errors (exit 64) are not wrapped in the envelope."},"224":{"id":"/cli-67","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#json-output","content":"The `errorType` field comes from a small, stable vocabulary, so scripts can\nbranch on the kind of failure: `auth`, `config`, `connection`, `context`,\n`import_schema`, `input_empty`, `input_missing`, `invalid_response`, `lookup`,\n`model`, `provider`, `rate_limit`, `runtime`, `streaming`, `truncated`, and\n`validation`."},"225":{"id":"/cli-68","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#exit-codes","content":"`0`: success."},"226":{"id":"/cli-69","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#exit-codes","content":"`1`: a runtime failure (network, provider, transcription), including a\nmeeting ID or title that matches nothing."},"227":{"id":"/cli-70","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#exit-codes","content":"`2`: an invalid value (unknown engine, format or provider, a missing\n`--model`), a missing or empty input file, or an ID prefix or title that is\nambiguous or too short."},"228":{"id":"/cli-71","page_id":"/cli","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/cli#exit-codes","content":"`64`: the command line itself couldn't be parsed (an unknown option or a\nmissing argument). These errors are printed as plain text, even with\n`--json`."},"229":{"id":"/day-journal","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"page","content":"Day Journal","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal"},"230":{"id":"/day-journal-0","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal","content":"Start a workday journal and Everpaper keeps a private history of your day — screenshots or an activity timeline, read on your Mac — then writes the day up for you to review."},"231":{"id":"/day-journal-1","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"Start your workday journal"},"232":{"id":"/day-journal-2","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Choose what your day keeps"},"233":{"id":"/day-journal-3","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#what-gets-captured","content":"What gets captured"},"234":{"id":"/day-journal-4","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#running-notes-and-the-days-entry","content":"Running notes and the day's entry"},"235":{"id":"/day-journal-5","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#the-end-of-day-review","content":"The end-of-day review"},"236":{"id":"/day-journal-6","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#during-meetings","content":"During meetings"},"237":{"id":"/day-journal-7","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#pausing-capture","content":"Pausing capture"},"238":{"id":"/day-journal-8","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#how-long-your-days-are-kept","content":"How long your days are kept"},"239":{"id":"/day-journal-9","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#todays-focus","content":"Today's focus"},"240":{"id":"/day-journal-10","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#related-to-whats-in-front","content":"Related to what's in front"},"241":{"id":"/day-journal-11","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#your-finished-days-timeline","content":"Your finished days (Timeline)"},"242":{"id":"/day-journal-12","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#where-your-data-is-stored","content":"Where your data is stored"},"243":{"id":"/day-journal-13","page_id":"/day-journal","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/day-journal#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"244":{"id":"/day-journal-14","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal","content":"You start the journal on **Today** (or **Capture → Open Day Journal**,\n⌘N), choose what it keeps in **Settings → Daily history**, and find\nfinished days in **Timeline**."},"245":{"id":"/day-journal-15","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal","content":"While it runs, Everpaper keeps a private record of your workday. In the default\nmode, Screen history, it takes a screenshot of each display every 2 minutes,\nreads the text on screen so you can find anything you saw, and writes the day\nup when you stop."},"246":{"id":"/day-journal-16","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"On **Today**, press **Start workday journal**. In Screen history or Detailed\nscreen history, macOS first needs Screen Recording. Press **Open Settings** and\nturn Everpaper on under **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Screen &\nSystem Audio Recording*&#x2A;. If the switch doesn't respond, remove Everpaper with\n&#x2A;*−*&#x2A; and add it again with &#x2A;*+**, then relaunch Everpaper. Everpaper must be\nin your Applications folder for macOS to keep the grant. Activity only needs\nno permission."},"247":{"id":"/day-journal-17","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"While the journal runs you'll see:"},"248":{"id":"/day-journal-18","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"A **RECORDING** indicator with an elapsed clock."},"249":{"id":"/day-journal-19","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"A running **FRAMES** count (screenshots taken so far)."},"250":{"id":"/day-journal-20","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"A **MOMENTS** count. Press **Mark Moment** to flag something worth\nremembering as it happens; you can add a short note to a moment, too."},"251":{"id":"/day-journal-21","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#start-your-workday-journal","content":"To wrap up, press **Stop & Review** (⌘R). **Discard** throws the\nday away, after asking."},"252":{"id":"/day-journal-22","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Pick a mode in **Settings → Daily history → History mode**. Setup uses slightly\ndifferent names; both are shown here."},"253":{"id":"/day-journal-23","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Mode"},"254":{"id":"/day-journal-24","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"What it keeps"},"255":{"id":"/day-journal-25","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Needs"},"256":{"id":"/day-journal-26","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"**Screen history** (Settings: Visual history), the default"},"257":{"id":"/day-journal-27","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"A screenshot of each display at your interval, read on this Mac"},"258":{"id":"/day-journal-28","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Screen Recording"},"259":{"id":"/day-journal-29","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"**Detailed screen history** (Settings: Adaptive visual history)"},"260":{"id":"/day-journal-30","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Screen history, plus extra images of the window you're focused on after meaningful changes"},"261":{"id":"/day-journal-31","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Screen Recording; Accessibility is optional and makes the extra images exact"},"262":{"id":"/day-journal-32","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"**Activity only** (Settings: Events only)"},"263":{"id":"/day-journal-33","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"A timeline of apps and windows. No screenshots"},"264":{"id":"/day-journal-34","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Nothing"},"265":{"id":"/day-journal-35","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"Detailed screen history keeps going while you read or watch without typing or\nclicking: at most one extra image every 30 seconds, and only when what's on\nscreen changed. Grant Accessibility for it in **Settings → General → Mac\npermissions**; the timed screenshots work without it."},"266":{"id":"/day-journal-36","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"If you used the earlier **Events + focused fallback** mode, Everpaper moved you\nto Detailed screen history. You can pick another mode at any time."},"267":{"id":"/day-journal-37","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#choose-what-your-day-keeps","content":"In every mode except Screen history you can also turn on **Computer History**,\nwhich records clicks, shortcuts and the text you select or type. It's off until\nyou turn it on. See Computer History."},"268":{"id":"/day-journal-38","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#what-gets-captured","content":"**Screenshots** (Screen history and Detailed screen history). An image of\neach whole display at the interval you choose: **every 2 minutes** by\ndefault, or 30 seconds, 1, 5 or 10 minutes (**Screenshot every**, shown in\nScreen history). It can\ninclude windows behind the one you're using."},"269":{"id":"/day-journal-39","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#what-gets-captured","content":"**What's left out.** Nothing is captured while what's in front is an app\nunder **Skip apps**, a site under **Skip sites**, or a private browsing\nwindow (**Skip private browsing windows**, on by default), all in\n**Settings → Privacy**. The timed screenshots and Detailed screen history's\nextra images follow the same rules. Nothing is captured while the display\nis asleep, and Detailed screen history's extra images also stop while the\nscreen is locked. See\nKeeping apps and sites out."},"270":{"id":"/day-journal-40","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#what-gets-captured","content":"**On-screen text.** Each screenshot is read on this Mac, so its text is\nsearchable."},"271":{"id":"/day-journal-41","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#what-gets-captured","content":"**Context.** The app and window in front, so activities are easy to make\nsense of later."},"272":{"id":"/day-journal-42","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#what-gets-captured","content":"**Capture focused text (deep read)** reads the focused window's text through\nAccessibility for richer recall. It's off by default and runs through the\nsame redaction as everything else. The text is stored on this Mac, and like\nother screen text your AI can read it. Turn it on under\n**Settings → Daily history → Advanced** (Screen history mode)."},"273":{"id":"/day-journal-43","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#running-notes-and-the-days-entry","content":"Every **10 minutes** by default (**Settings → Daily history → Review new\nactivity every**: 10, 15, 30 or 60 minutes), your AI reviews what's new and\nadds to the day's running notes. The notes build up through the day, and get\none full tidy-up in the evening."},"274":{"id":"/day-journal-44","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#running-notes-and-the-days-entry","content":"The running notes wait while you record a meeting, in Low Power Mode, when\nthe Mac is running hot, and on battery if **Reduce work on battery** is on.\nOther background AI work, the kind nobody is waiting on, waits for a quiet\nmoment; while it does, Today shows why, for example **Paused: microphone in\nuse by** and the app's name. Anything you ask for still goes first, and work\nwith a deadline still gets done. **Settings → General → AI work** shows the\nsame status as **Background AI**, and **AI use today** shows how much each\nfeature used the AI today. See\nWhen AI work runs."},"275":{"id":"/day-journal-45","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#running-notes-and-the-days-entry","content":"The running notes, the day's entry, Decisions and Commitments, and answers to\nyour questions use your AI. Set it up under **Settings → AI & summaries → AI\nconnection**; an on-device option keeps all of it on your Mac. See\nAI on your Mac. Capture, text recognition, search and\nstorage never need AI."},"276":{"id":"/day-journal-46","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#the-end-of-day-review","content":"Press **Stop & Review** (⌘R). Everpaper finishes its notes, then\nopens **Here's the day** on Today. Read the running notes, answer any\nquestions, add notes for the day, and press **Save Journal**. (**Discard**\ndeletes the whole day — its observations, screenshots and your answers — and\ncan't be undone.)"},"277":{"id":"/day-journal-47","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#the-end-of-day-review","content":"On save, your AI writes the day's entry: a first-person diary of what you did,\nincluding any meetings you recorded that day. It appears as **Day Summary** on\nthat day's page in Timeline. If no AI is set up, the day is still saved without\nan entry; once you set up AI, the day's page offers **Write up this day**. A\nday cut short by a crash or force-quit is written up automatically once\nEverpaper can."},"278":{"id":"/day-journal-48","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#the-end-of-day-review","content":"**Journal threads** (**Settings → AI & summaries → Your memory & summaries**,\noff by default) groups the day's moments by topic, picks the most telling ones\nwhen a day is too long to send in full, and lets the evening entry recall a\nfew related moments from earlier days. In testing it made the entry more\nfactual and less personal, which is why it starts off. When it's on, a second\nswitch, &#x2A;*Evening threads (experimental)**, appears beneath it."},"279":{"id":"/day-journal-49","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#during-meetings","content":"While you record a meeting, Screen history and Activity only pause on their\nown and resume when the meeting ends. Detailed screen history keeps taking its\nextra images during the meeting, with your skip rules applied. Clicks and\ntyped text stay paused in every mode. You can still mark moments. What was said in the meeting is\nincluded in that evening's entry. If you press **Stop & Review** while a\nmeeting is still recording, your day is prepared while the meeting carries on."},"280":{"id":"/day-journal-50","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#pausing-capture","content":"Press **Pause** to stop capture for a while. You can note why with a quick\nreason — **Meeting**, **Break**, **Lunch**, **Personal** — or type your own.\nPress **Resume** to start again. The pause and its reason are recorded, so a\nfinished day shows when and why capture stopped. The Everpaper menu-bar icon\nhas **Pause Journal** and **Resume Journal** too."},"281":{"id":"/day-journal-51","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#pausing-capture","content":"Everpaper can also pause on its own:"},"282":{"id":"/day-journal-52","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#pausing-capture","content":"**Pause when you’re away** stops screenshots when you step away. It is on by\ndefault, after **2 minutes** (or 30 seconds, 1 minute), and appears in Screen\nhistory."},"283":{"id":"/day-journal-53","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#pausing-capture","content":"**Reduce work on battery** lightens capture and analysis on battery. Off by\ndefault."},"284":{"id":"/day-journal-54","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#pausing-capture","content":"Both are in **Settings → Daily history → Capture schedule**. Nothing is\ncaptured while the display is asleep, and Detailed screen history's extra\nimages also stop while the screen is locked."},"285":{"id":"/day-journal-55","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#how-long-your-days-are-kept","content":"**Keep screenshots for** (**Settings → Daily history → How long it stays**)\ndeletes screenshots older than **30 days** by default (or 7, 90 days, or\nForever). In Detailed screen history the setting reads **Keep checkpoints\nfor**; in Activity only, **Keep visual captures for**.\nThe same choice is also in **Settings → Privacy → How long it stays**, as\n**Keep screenshot images for**, with the switch below under &#x2A;*Manage saved\ntext…** as **Also delete expired text & recall data**."},"286":{"id":"/day-journal-56","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#how-long-your-days-are-kept","content":"On a new install, **Also delete their text & recall data** is on. Past the\nsame limit, Everpaper also deletes that day's recognized text, search data,\nrunning notes and written entry. Some of the day, such as the app timeline and\nthe notes you typed in the review, can stay; to remove everything, delete the\nday. To keep your written days, turn that switch off or choose Forever before\nthe limit passes. Deleted days can't be restored."},"287":{"id":"/day-journal-57","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#how-long-your-days-are-kept","content":"If you upgraded from an earlier build that already had journal data, the\nswitch starts off and only images are removed. Meetings are not affected."},"288":{"id":"/day-journal-58","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#todays-focus","content":"**Today's focus** on the Today page suggests a few to-dos. Without AI it finds\n**open loops** (files or topics you touched, then dropped) and **cooling\nthreads** (things that went quiet). With AI set up, it also pulls to-dos from\nyour recent meetings and days, and turns the action items in your meeting\nresults into tasks. These appear first."},"289":{"id":"/day-journal-59","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#todays-focus","content":"You can check a to-do off, dismiss it, or press **Add to Reminders**. Each\nto-do becomes its own reminder in a Reminders list called **Everpaper** and\nstays open in Today. The first time, macOS asks for access to Reminders.\n**View all tasks** shows the full list."},"290":{"id":"/day-journal-60","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#related-to-whats-in-front","content":"When a document stays in front for a little while, Today can show a quiet\n**RELATED TO** line naming it, with up to three related past moments, meetings\nor files. Click one to open it, or ✕ to hide them. There are no\nnotifications, and skipped apps, skipped sites and private windows never\ntrigger it. Turn it off with **Show related moments** in **Settings →\nSpeech**."},"291":{"id":"/day-journal-61","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#your-finished-days-timeline","content":"Finished days live in **Timeline** in the sidebar. Each page shows the **Day\nSummary**, what you did and when, your captures, and your notes. The side rail\nlists the day's **Decisions** and **Commitments** (with AI), people and\nprojects, open threads, and your rhythm. &#x2A;*Ask this day…** answers questions\nabout that day only. To remove a day, use **Delete this day and all its\nevidence**; you can undo it from Today right after."},"292":{"id":"/day-journal-62","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#your-finished-days-timeline","content":"Use ←/→ to turn pages and ⌘D to jump to a\ndate. **Ask the book** (⌘F) at the top of Timeline searches across\nevery day; see Recall."},"293":{"id":"/day-journal-63","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#your-finished-days-timeline","content":"Press ⌘L for the **Day Index** — a chronological overview of every\ncaptured day, newest first. Each row shows the day's title, date, frame count,\nand a thumbnail of its most recent capture. Use ↑/↓ to\nmove and Return to turn straight to a day. A density strip at the\ntop shows how many days you've captured and the span of your history."},"294":{"id":"/day-journal-64","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#your-finished-days-timeline","content":"The red ribbon at the top right, or ⌘T, always brings you back to\nToday."},"295":{"id":"/day-journal-65","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#where-your-data-is-stored","content":"Your screenshots, text, timeline, entries and notes are stored on this Mac, in\nEverpaper's folder in your user Library. To keep a copy elsewhere, use\nExport."},"296":{"id":"/day-journal-66","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#where-your-data-is-stored","content":"Capture and text recognition happen on this Mac. Text leaves it only if you set\nup an AI that sends it, or let another AI app read your journal; see\nAI on your Mac."},"297":{"id":"/day-journal-67","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#related-reading","content":"Microsoft Recall for Mac: how screen history compares with Windows Recall."},"298":{"id":"/day-journal-68","page_id":"/day-journal","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/day-journal#related-reading","content":"Limitless and Rewind alternatives: what to use after Rewind stopped capturing."},"299":{"id":"/export","page_id":"/export","type":"page","content":"Export","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/export"},"300":{"id":"/export-0","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export","content":"Turn your days into an Obsidian-style vault of linked Markdown notes or a knowledge graph in GraphML and Mermaid, and save any meeting's transcript or audio. Everything stays on your Mac."},"301":{"id":"/export-1","page_id":"/export","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"Export an Obsidian vault"},"302":{"id":"/export-2","page_id":"/export","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/export#export-a-graph","content":"Export a graph"},"303":{"id":"/export-3","page_id":"/export","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/export#exporting-meetings","content":"Exporting meetings"},"304":{"id":"/export-4","page_id":"/export","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/export#where-the-files-land","content":"Where the files land"},"305":{"id":"/export-5","page_id":"/export","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/export#before-you-export","content":"Before you export"},"306":{"id":"/export-6","page_id":"/export","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/export#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"307":{"id":"/export-7","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export","content":"Export turns what Everpaper has already captured into open, portable files you\ncan browse, link, and visualize in other tools. Nothing new leaves your machine\n— export only writes out the on-device data you can already see in the app.\nExport is a one-way snapshot you can re-run any time."},"308":{"id":"/export-8","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export","content":"You'll find it in **Memory** (also called Second Brain) in the sidebar\n(⌘4 also opens it). Choose the **Export** tab (⌥⌘6)."},"309":{"id":"/export-9","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**Export Obsidian vault** writes your whole journal as a folder of linked\nMarkdown notes — the kind of vault Obsidian, Logseq, or any plain-Markdown editor\ncan open directly."},"310":{"id":"/export-10","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"Each day becomes a daily note, and the people, sites, and files you\nencountered become their own notes, joined together with `[[wikilinks]]` so the\nwhole thing browses as a connected web."},"311":{"id":"/export-11","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"What you get:"},"312":{"id":"/export-12","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**Days/**: one note per captured day, with the day's narrative, a timeline of\nwhat you worked on, and linked lists of the **People**, **Links**, and **Files**\nseen that day. Your own notes for the day come along too. Each note carries\nfrontmatter (`date`, `captures`, `tags`)."},"313":{"id":"/export-13","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**People/**: one note per person, built from the email addresses in your\nhistory. Addresses are humanized into names (`jane.smith@example.com` becomes\n*Jane Smith*), and misread copies of the same address collapse into a single\nnote. Each note lists the days that person showed up."},"314":{"id":"/export-14","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**Links/**: one note per web address seen, backlinked to the days it\nappeared."},"315":{"id":"/export-15","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**Files/**: one note per file, backlinked to the days it appeared."},"316":{"id":"/export-16","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**Topics/**: \"area\" notes for the clusters Everpaper detected in your graph,\neach linking its members."},"317":{"id":"/export-17","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"**GRAPH\\_REPORT.md**: an overview of the vault: your most-connected\nnodes, surprising connections, and a few questions worth exploring, all\nresolving to the notes above."},"318":{"id":"/export-18","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-an-obsidian-vault","content":"Finished days are included, and so is a day you've stopped but haven't reviewed\nyet. Every note is plain Markdown — no lock-in. Re-running the export refreshes\nthe vault in place."},"319":{"id":"/export-19","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-a-graph","content":"**Export graph (GraphML + Mermaid)** writes your knowledge graph — the people,\nsites, and files that recur together — in two visualization-ready formats:"},"320":{"id":"/export-20","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-a-graph","content":"**graph.graphml**: open it in yEd,\nGephi, or Obsidian's graph plugins for an interactive,\nlaid-out view."},"321":{"id":"/export-21","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-a-graph","content":"**graph.mermaid**: a Mermaid `graph TD` diagram you\ncan paste straight into Markdown, Obsidian, or Notion, or render at\nmermaid.live."},"322":{"id":"/export-22","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#export-a-graph","content":"Both are derived from the same snapshot Memory's **Connections** tab shows:\nnodes are the things you keep returning to, and edges are the links between\nthings that keep appearing together (weighted by how strong the connection is)."},"323":{"id":"/export-23","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#exporting-meetings","content":"The vault covers your days, not your meetings. To export a meeting, open it and\npress **Export** to save its transcript as .txt, .md, .srt, .vtt or .json, or\n**Audio** to save its recording as an .m4a file. Everpaper asks where to save\neach one. In the Library, each row has &#x2A;*Save Transcript…** and &#x2A;*Save Audio…**.\nTo send a meeting's to-dos to Reminders, use **Add to Reminders** in Today's\nfocus. See also Meetings and Command line."},"324":{"id":"/export-24","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#exporting-meetings","content":"Your word list can be saved too: in Settings → **Speech** → **Your words &\nphrases**, **Backup** has &#x2A;*Export…**."},"325":{"id":"/export-25","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#where-the-files-land","content":"By default the vault and graph are written inside Everpaper's own folder in\nyour user Library. After an export runs, a **Reveal in Finder** button appears\nnext to it, the quickest way to jump to the files. The status line below the buttons confirms\nwhat was written (for example, &#x2A;Exported 12 days · 34 people · 18 links · 9\nfiles.* for the vault, or &#x2A;Exported graph · 60 nodes · 142 edges (GraphML +\nMermaid).* for the graph)."},"326":{"id":"/export-26","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#before-you-export","content":"Export needs something to export, so journal a few days first. With\nnothing captured yet, the status line reads &#x2A;Exported 0 days…*."},"327":{"id":"/export-27","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#before-you-export","content":"On a new install, Everpaper deletes a day's written entry and recognized text\nafter your screenshot limit (30 days by default; see\nHow long your days are kept). Older\ndays then export with only their timeline and your notes. Export before then,\nor change that setting, if you want full notes for older days."},"328":{"id":"/export-28","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#before-you-export","content":"Export is fully local. It reuses only data Everpaper has already captured on\nyour Mac, and nothing is sent anywhere. Secrets such as card numbers, keys and\none-time codes are removed, but names, email addresses, links and file paths\nare kept. They are what make the vault useful. Keep the exported folder as\nprivate as your journal. The files are yours to move, edit, and back up\nhowever you like."},"329":{"id":"/export-29","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#related-reading","content":"Best Obsidian alternatives: where the Obsidian vault export fits."},"330":{"id":"/export-30","page_id":"/export","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/export#related-reading","content":"Obsidian canvas alternatives: what to open the graph export in."},"331":{"id":"/getting-started","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting started","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started"},"332":{"id":"/getting-started-0","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started","content":"Join the private beta, install Everpaper, walk through setup, and grant the permissions it needs."},"333":{"id":"/getting-started-1","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"334":{"id":"/getting-started-2","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Join the beta and install"},"335":{"id":"/getting-started-3","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#first-time-setup","content":"First-time setup"},"336":{"id":"/getting-started-4","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#welcome","content":"Welcome"},"337":{"id":"/getting-started-5","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#1-your-memory","content":"1\\. Your memory"},"338":{"id":"/getting-started-6","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"2\\. Daily history"},"339":{"id":"/getting-started-7","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"3\\. Access"},"340":{"id":"/getting-started-8","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#4-private-summaries","content":"4\\. Private summaries"},"341":{"id":"/getting-started-9","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"5\\. Your setup"},"342":{"id":"/getting-started-10","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#when-you-open-everpaper","content":"When you open Everpaper"},"343":{"id":"/getting-started-11","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#finding-your-way","content":"Finding your way"},"344":{"id":"/getting-started-12","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#granting-screen-recording-on-recent-macos","content":"Granting Screen Recording on recent macOS"},"345":{"id":"/getting-started-13","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#changing-things-later","content":"Changing things later"},"346":{"id":"/getting-started-14","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/getting-started#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"347":{"id":"/getting-started-15","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started","content":"Everpaper is in private beta. This page covers joining, installing, and the\nshort setup that runs the first time you open it."},"348":{"id":"/getting-started-16","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#requirements","content":"**macOS 15 (Sequoia) or later.**"},"349":{"id":"/getting-started-17","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#requirements","content":"**Apple silicon** (M-series). Everpaper's speech and AI models run on Apple\nsilicon's Neural Engine and GPU. It does not run on Intel Macs."},"350":{"id":"/getting-started-18","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#requirements","content":"**For Everpaper Native, the built-in private AI: macOS 27.** With 16 GB of\nmemory or more it runs Gemma 4 E4B; with less, Qwen3 4B. On macOS 15 and 26,\nsetup installs a managed oMLX model instead (Gemma 4 E4B from 24 GB of\nmemory, a smaller model below that), or uses an LM Studio or Ollama you\nalready run. See AI on your Mac."},"351":{"id":"/getting-started-19","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#requirements","content":"**Free disk space for the on-device models:** about 1 GB for meeting\ntranscription, plus about 2 to 9 GB for the private AI model, depending on\nyour Mac. Gemma 4 E4B in Everpaper Native needs about 16 GB free while it\ninstalls and about 8.5 GB afterwards. The search model adds about 1.5 GB\non macOS 27, and less on earlier macOS."},"352":{"id":"/getting-started-20","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#requirements","content":"**Downloads.** Nothing downloads during setup until you press **Prepare on\nthis Mac**. After setup, the search model sets itself up in the background\nat a quiet moment. **Set up later** or **Cancel preparation** puts that off\nfor a week. See Search by meaning."},"353":{"id":"/getting-started-21","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Apply at everpaper.app/beta. If you're\nselected, you'll hear back within 48 hours."},"354":{"id":"/getting-started-22","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Each build reaches you as a private download link to a disk image named\nafter its version. Please don't share the link."},"355":{"id":"/getting-started-23","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Open the disk image and drag **Everpaper** onto the **Applications** folder\nshortcut."},"356":{"id":"/getting-started-24","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Open **Everpaper** from Applications."},"357":{"id":"/getting-started-25","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Always run Everpaper from the Applications folder, not from the disk image or\nDownloads. Otherwise macOS can't keep the Screen Recording permission."},"358":{"id":"/getting-started-26","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"During the private beta Everpaper does not update itself. Each new build\narrives as a new link, and you install it over the old copy; your history,\nsettings and models stay in place. See Updates & Support."},"359":{"id":"/getting-started-27","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#join-the-beta-and-install","content":"Used a Hindsight-branded build of this app before? Everpaper keeps the same\ndata, so there's nothing to import. Coming from the original Hindsight app?\n&#x2A;*Settings → General → Setup & data → Import from Hindsight (legacy)** copies\nits data into Everpaper and leaves the originals untouched."},"360":{"id":"/getting-started-28","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#first-time-setup","content":"The first time you open Everpaper, a welcome page opens, then setup. Setup has\nup to five steps (four if you choose only meetings), and each page turns to\nthe next like a page in a book. A pill at the top right names the step and\ncounts it, for example **Your memory · 1 of 5**. **Back** is at the bottom\nleft, and Esc also goes back one page. Only the first step needs\nan answer: you can move past every other step and finish it later in\nSettings. If you quit halfway, setup reopens where you left off."},"361":{"id":"/getting-started-29","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#first-time-setup","content":"Moving through the pages changes nothing on its own. A setting is saved only\nwhen you pick something, and nothing downloads until you press **Prepare on\nthis Mac**. With **Reduce motion** on, pages fade instead of turning. With\n**Reduce transparency** on, or before macOS 26, pages show plain paper instead\nof glass."},"362":{"id":"/getting-started-30","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#welcome","content":"**A searchable memory of your work.** One page shows what Everpaper keeps:\n**Workdays you start** and **Meetings you record**, processed on this Mac by\ndefault. Press **Set up Everpaper** to begin."},"363":{"id":"/getting-started-31","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#1-your-memory","content":"**What would you like to remember?** Choose **My meetings**, **My days** or\n**Both** (or press 1, 2 or 3). You can add the rest later in Settings."},"364":{"id":"/getting-started-32","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#1-your-memory","content":"Nothing records automatically: you decide when to start and stop."},"365":{"id":"/getting-started-33","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"Skipped if you chose **My meetings**."},"366":{"id":"/getting-started-34","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"**How should your day be remembered?** This is what Everpaper may observe while\na workday journal is running:"},"367":{"id":"/getting-started-35","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"**Screen history** (the default): full-display screenshots at your chosen\ninterval, read on this Mac so you can search what you saw. They use more\nstorage and can include windows behind the one you're using."},"368":{"id":"/getting-started-36","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"**Detailed screen history**: Screen history plus extra images of the window\nyou're focused on."},"369":{"id":"/getting-started-37","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"**Activity only**: a timeline of apps and windows, with no screenshots."},"370":{"id":"/getting-started-38","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"Capture starts only when you start a workday journal. The\nDay Journal page compares the modes."},"371":{"id":"/getting-started-39","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#2-daily-history","content":"**Clicks, selections, and typed text** (beta; any mode except Screen history).\nOff until you turn on **Computer History events & text**. When it's on,\nEverpaper remembers clicks, shortcuts, selected text and typed text in apps you\nhaven't excluded, which can include email and messages. Typed text is kept as\nan encrypted, redacted record, and the original text expires after 48 hours.\nPassword fields and private browsing are always excluded. Everything is stored\non this Mac. Your AI reads it to write your day, and a cloud AI needs a\nseparate consent. This opt-in also asks\nfor **Accessibility** and **Input Monitoring** in the next step. See\nComputer History."},"372":{"id":"/getting-started-40","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"**A little access, for a clear reason.** Your Mac asks for each permission\nseparately. Allow only what you want to use; anything you put off stays\nunavailable until you turn it on in Settings. You only see the rows your\nchoices need:"},"373":{"id":"/getting-started-41","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"**Screen and system audio**: for meetings (to hear the other side of a call)\nand for Screen history or Detailed screen history. Press **Allow access**.\nOnce it's granted, macOS also asks separately for **System Audio\nRecording**, a lighter way for meetings to hear the call."},"374":{"id":"/getting-started-42","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"**Microphone**: for meetings. Press **Allow microphone**."},"375":{"id":"/getting-started-43","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"**Accessibility** and **Input Monitoring**: only if you turned on Computer\nHistory."},"376":{"id":"/getting-started-44","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"**Accessibility**, marked **OPTIONAL**, with Detailed screen history: it\nadds exact images of the focused window. The timed screenshots work without\nit."},"377":{"id":"/getting-started-45","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"Each button asks macOS directly. It reads &#x2A;*Waiting for macOS…** while the\nsystem dialog is open, then **Allowed**. If the request isn't granted, it\nturns into **Open System Settings** instead of asking again."},"378":{"id":"/getting-started-46","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#3-access","content":"With Activity only and no meetings, there's nothing to grant. Granting a\npermission does not start recording. If the status doesn't update, see\nGranting Screen Recording."},"379":{"id":"/getting-started-47","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#4-private-summaries","content":"**Private summaries, on your Mac.** A card headed **Recommended for this\nMac** shows one setup, with a status line each for **Meetings** (if you chose\nthem), **Summaries** and **Search**. If you already have an AI setup, it's\nkept. If LM Studio or Ollama is already running with a chat model, it's used\nas it is. Otherwise:"},"380":{"id":"/getting-started-48","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#4-private-summaries","content":"**Everpaper Native** on macOS 27: Gemma 4 E4B with 16 GB of memory or more,\nQwen3 4B below that."},"381":{"id":"/getting-started-49","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#4-private-summaries","content":"**Managed oMLX** on earlier macOS: Everpaper installs oMLX and a model sized\nfor your Mac."},"382":{"id":"/getting-started-50","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#4-private-summaries","content":"If you chose meetings, the same step also prepares meeting transcription and\nlive speaker labels. **Prepare on this Mac** also sets up the search model\n(see Search by meaning). Nothing downloads until\nyou press it, and you can keep going while it runs; the search model carries\non preparing in the background after you move on. **Cancel preparation**\nstops it."},"383":{"id":"/getting-started-51","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#4-private-summaries","content":"**Set up later** skips all of it: recording and your journal still work, your\nfirst meeting downloads the transcription model, and the search model waits a\nweek before it sets itself up in the background. **Choose advanced options**\nlists every route, including **Use my own provider** (a cloud service or your\nown endpoint) and **No AI for now**; **Use recommended setup** takes you back\nto the card. Press **Review my setup** to continue.\nAI on your Mac explains each option."},"384":{"id":"/getting-started-52","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"**Your Everpaper, ready when you are.** A receipt of what you chose, one line\neach. For your days: **Your workday**, plus **Clicks and text** with Detailed\nscreen history or Activity only. For meetings: **Your conversations** and\n**Meeting transcripts**. Then **Summaries and questions** and **Your\nprivacy**. Each line except Your privacy says honestly where it stands:"},"385":{"id":"/getting-started-53","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"**Ready**"},"386":{"id":"/getting-started-54","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"**Preparing**: still downloading or getting ready in the background."},"387":{"id":"/getting-started-55","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"**Set up later**"},"388":{"id":"/getting-started-56","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"**Needs permission**: a permission it needs wasn't granted."},"389":{"id":"/getting-started-57","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#5-your-setup","content":"A counter such as **3 of 4 ready** sits at the top, and a bookmark appears\nonly when everything you chose is really ready. **YOUR FIRST MOMENT**\nsuggests where to begin. Press **Open Everpaper**."},"390":{"id":"/getting-started-58","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#when-you-open-everpaper","content":"You land on **Today**, or on **Meetings** if you chose My meetings. Finishing\nsetup never starts a recording or a workday journal:"},"391":{"id":"/getting-started-59","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#when-you-open-everpaper","content":"On **Today**, press **Start workday journal** when you begin work."},"392":{"id":"/getting-started-60","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#when-you-open-everpaper","content":"In **Meetings**, press **Record** when a conversation starts, and tell the\nother people you're recording."},"393":{"id":"/getting-started-61","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#finding-your-way","content":"The sidebar has six places, and ⌘K opens the Index. See\nFinding your way."},"394":{"id":"/getting-started-62","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#granting-screen-recording-on-recent-macos","content":"Meeting recording and the screen history modes rely on the **Screen & System\nAudio Recording** permission. On recent macOS, granting it has one quirk worth\nknowing."},"395":{"id":"/getting-started-63","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#granting-screen-recording-on-recent-macos","content":"In the **Access** step, on the **Screen and system audio** row, press\n**Allow access** (or **Open System Settings**). This adds Everpaper to the\nlist and opens **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Screen & System\nAudio Recording**."},"396":{"id":"/getting-started-64","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#granting-screen-recording-on-recent-macos","content":"**Toggle Everpaper on.** On recent macOS there's no confirmation dialog —\nflipping the toggle is the grant."},"397":{"id":"/getting-started-65","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#granting-screen-recording-on-recent-macos","content":"**Relaunch Everpaper.** macOS only applies this permission when the app\nstarts, so the status may not change until you quit and reopen. Setup shows\na **Relaunch Everpaper** button when it notices the grant hasn't taken\neffect yet."},"398":{"id":"/getting-started-66","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#granting-screen-recording-on-recent-macos","content":"If the entry doesn't respond, remove it from the list with &#x2A;*−*&#x2A;, add\nEverpaper from your Applications folder again with &#x2A;*+**, then relaunch. If\nsetup says Everpaper is running outside Applications, move it there first:\nmacOS can't keep the grant otherwise."},"399":{"id":"/getting-started-67","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#changing-things-later","content":"Open **Settings** (⌘,). **General → Mac permissions** shows the\nmicrophone, Screen & System Audio and Accessibility. **Meetings → During a\nmeeting → System audio route** shows whether meetings use the lighter System\nAudio Recording, with **Allow now** or **Check again**. **Meetings →\nCalendar** has calendar access. **Daily history** has the permissions for\nclicks and typed text. **AI & summaries → Files you include → Search model**\nchooses the search model. To walk through setup again, use **General → Setup &\ndata → Run setup again**; there, **Return to Everpaper** (or Esc)\ncloses it, and **Back** is ⌘\\[."},"400":{"id":"/getting-started-68","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#related-reading","content":"What is Everpaper: requirements, features and privacy defaults on one page."},"401":{"id":"/getting-started-69","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#related-reading","content":"Everpaper b101: the launcher, Dictate and clipboard history."},"402":{"id":"/","page_id":"/","type":"page","content":"Welcome","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/"},"403":{"id":"/-0","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Everpaper is a private memory of your workdays and meetings on your Mac — Today, Meetings, Timeline, Library and Memory — processed on this Mac by default."},"404":{"id":"/-1","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"Finding your way"},"405":{"id":"/-2","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#whats-inside","content":"What's inside"},"406":{"id":"/-3","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#today-and-timeline","content":"Today and Timeline"},"407":{"id":"/-4","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#meetings","content":"Meetings"},"408":{"id":"/-5","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#memory-second-brain","content":"Memory (Second Brain)"},"409":{"id":"/-6","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#also-in-this-beta","content":"Also in this beta"},"410":{"id":"/-7","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#privacy","content":"Privacy"},"411":{"id":"/-8","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#get-started","content":"Get started"},"412":{"id":"/-9","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"413":{"id":"/-10","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Everpaper is a private memory of your workdays and meetings, on your Mac. Start\na workday journal and it keeps a searchable history of what you worked on.\nRecord a meeting and it keeps the audio, a transcript and a summary. Later, ask\nit what you need and it answers with the source."},"414":{"id":"/-11","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Everything you capture is stored and processed on this Mac by default. Nothing\ngoes to a cloud service unless you connect one and separately allow it."},"415":{"id":"/-12","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Everpaper is in private beta. Getting started explains how\nto join and install it."},"416":{"id":"/-13","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"The sidebar has six places:"},"417":{"id":"/-14","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"**Today**: your day so far, the journal control, your next meeting and\nToday's focus."},"418":{"id":"/-15","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"**Meetings**: record and review conversations."},"419":{"id":"/-16","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"**Timeline**: your finished days, one per page."},"420":{"id":"/-17","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"**Library**: every meeting recording and imported audio file."},"421":{"id":"/-18","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"**Memory** (also called Second Brain): ask questions across everything, and\nsee what Everpaper has learned about your work."},"422":{"id":"/-19","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"**Settings**."},"423":{"id":"/-20","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"Everpaper treats your history as a book. That's where the small second names\nunder three of these places come from (The Days, The Archive, Second Brain),\nand why the Index files the beliefs Memory has formed under Commonplace Book."},"424":{"id":"/-21","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#finding-your-way","content":"Press ⌘K for the Index to jump to any day, meeting, setting or\ncommand. On Timeline, the arrow keys turn between days. The red ribbon at the\ntop right of every other page, or ⌘T, brings you back to Today. From\nany app, ⌥Space opens the Concordance, a quick find-and-ask panel."},"425":{"id":"/-22","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#today-and-timeline","content":"Press **Start workday journal** on Today when you begin work. Nothing is\ncaptured until you do. While it runs, Everpaper keeps a private history in the\nmode you chose (Screen history, Detailed screen history or Activity only).\nPress **Stop & Review** and it writes up your day. Finished days live in\n**Timeline**, one per page: turn with the arrow keys, use **Ask the book**\n(⌘F) to search across every day, or &#x2A;*Ask this day…** on one page.\nOn Today, &#x2A;*Ask your memory…** asks across everything, and ⇧⌘A\ntakes you there from any page."},"426":{"id":"/-23","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#today-and-timeline","content":"Read more about the Day Journal →"},"427":{"id":"/-24","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#meetings","content":"Meetings records and transcribes your conversations on this Mac, with live\ncaptions and speaker labels. Start with **Record** on the Meetings page,\n**Record now** on Today, ⇧⌘M from any app, the menu-bar icon, or\n⌘K → **Begin meeting**. If you allow calendar access, Everpaper can\nremind you before meetings (by default, those with a video-call link), or start\nrecording automatically. With AI set up, each finished meeting gets an\nautomatic Summary. Meetings are saved to your Library with a title you can\nrename."},"428":{"id":"/-25","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#meetings","content":"Read more about Meetings →"},"429":{"id":"/-26","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#memory-second-brain","content":"Memory learns from what you capture. **Ask** questions across your days,\nmeetings and files; see what it has learned about **You**; turn **Insights** into a draft email or follow-up event; explore\n**Connections** between people, projects and ideas; and **Export** everything\nas an Obsidian vault or a graph."},"430":{"id":"/-27","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#memory-second-brain","content":"Read more about Memory →"},"431":{"id":"/-28","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#also-in-this-beta","content":"**Private AI on your Mac**: Everpaper Native on macOS 27 (Gemma 4 E4B with\n16 GB of memory or more), or a managed local model on earlier macOS. See\nAI on your Mac."},"432":{"id":"/-29","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#also-in-this-beta","content":"**The Concordance**: press ⌥Space in any app to find or ask about\na day, a meeting or a file."},"433":{"id":"/-30","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#also-in-this-beta","content":"**Search by meaning**: an on-device search model finds things described in\nother words or another language; on macOS 27, also screenshots by what they\nshow and meetings by what was heard. See\nSearch by meaning."},"434":{"id":"/-31","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#also-in-this-beta","content":"**Clicks, selections, and typed text** (Computer History): beta, off until\nyou turn it on. See Privacy."},"435":{"id":"/-32","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#privacy","content":"Everpaper is on-device by default:"},"436":{"id":"/-33","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#privacy","content":"**Capture, transcription, and storage stay local.** Meetings are transcribed\non your Mac, and your journal database never leaves it."},"437":{"id":"/-34","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#privacy","content":"**No AI traffic without a provider you choose.** If you don't set one up,\nnothing is sent to any AI service. Recording, transcription, search and your\njournal still work; written summaries and answers wait until you set one up."},"438":{"id":"/-35","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#privacy","content":"**Local AI keeps everything on your Mac.** Setup can prepare a private model\nfor you: Everpaper Native on macOS 27, or a managed oMLX model on earlier\nmacOS. It can also use an LM Studio or Ollama you already run. Your text is\nprocessed locally, with no calls off the Mac."},"439":{"id":"/-36","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#privacy","content":"**Cloud is opt-in.** Nothing goes to a cloud AI until you connect one and\nturn on **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** (Settings → AI &\nsummaries; in Settings → Privacy it's called **Allow online journal\nanalysis**). The same switch covers journal text,\nmeeting transcripts, questions and notes. Before anything is sent, secrets\nsuch as keys and card numbers, and contact details such as email addresses\nand phone numbers, are redacted."},"440":{"id":"/-37","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#get-started","content":"Head to Getting started to join the private beta, install\nEverpaper and walk through setup."},"441":{"id":"/-38","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#related-reading","content":"What is Everpaper: the product facts on one page."},"442":{"id":"/-39","page_id":"/","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/#related-reading","content":"The blog: comparisons with other tools, and notes on privacy and the on-device engineering."},"443":{"id":"/meetings","page_id":"/meetings","type":"page","content":"Meetings","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings"},"444":{"id":"/meetings-0","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings","content":"Record and transcribe meetings on your Mac: a live panel with notes, captions and Ask, speaker names, and an automatic summary."},"445":{"id":"/meetings-1","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"Start a recording"},"446":{"id":"/meetings-2","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"Audio and meeting settings"},"447":{"id":"/meetings-3","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"The live panel"},"448":{"id":"/meetings-4","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#ask-during-a-meeting","content":"Ask during a meeting"},"449":{"id":"/meetings-5","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#the-floating-pill","content":"The floating pill"},"450":{"id":"/meetings-6","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#after-a-meeting","content":"After a meeting"},"451":{"id":"/meetings-7","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#everyday-or-detailed","content":"Everyday or Detailed"},"452":{"id":"/meetings-8","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#the-automatic-summary","content":"The automatic summary"},"453":{"id":"/meetings-9","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#templates-and-marked-prompts","content":"Templates and marked prompts"},"454":{"id":"/meetings-10","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#speaker-names","content":"Speaker names"},"455":{"id":"/meetings-11","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#hiding-speakers","content":"Hiding speakers"},"456":{"id":"/meetings-12","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#to-dos-from-a-meeting","content":"To-dos from a meeting"},"457":{"id":"/meetings-13","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#privacy","content":"Privacy"},"458":{"id":"/meetings-14","page_id":"/meetings","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/meetings#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"459":{"id":"/meetings-15","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings","content":"Meetings is where Everpaper records, transcribes and summarizes your\nconversations. Recording and transcription happen on your Mac, and recordings\nare never uploaded. Each finished meeting is saved to your Library so you can\ncome back to it."},"460":{"id":"/meetings-16","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"**Meetings page**: click **Record** on the **Record a meeting** tile."},"461":{"id":"/meetings-17","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"**Today**: click **Record now** on the **Next meeting** card. The recording\nis named after your next calendar event if there is one."},"462":{"id":"/meetings-18","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"**Hotkey**: press ⇧⌘M from any app; press it again to stop.\nChange it in **Settings → Meetings → Meeting hotkey**."},"463":{"id":"/meetings-19","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"**Menu bar**: click the Everpaper icon and choose **Start Recording**."},"464":{"id":"/meetings-20","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"**Index**: press ⌘K and choose **Begin meeting** (it reads **End\nmeeting** while you're recording)."},"465":{"id":"/meetings-21","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"**Calendar**: Everpaper can remind you or start recording when a meeting\nbegins. See Calendar Auto-Start."},"466":{"id":"/meetings-22","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"Everpaper needs **Screen & System Audio Recording** access (that is how macOS\nlets it hear the call) and, unless you chose System Audio Only, **Microphone**\naccess. If one is missing, it opens the right pane of System Settings. Keep\nEverpaper in your Applications folder, or macOS won't remember the grant."},"467":{"id":"/meetings-23","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"Before your first meeting, never during one, macOS also asks for **System\nAudio Recording**, a lighter way for Everpaper to hear the call. It isn't\nrequired: if you decline, Everpaper records the call through screen capture as\nbefore and tells you so. Check or change it under **System audio route** in\n**Settings → Meetings → During a meeting** (**Allow now**, or **Check again**\nafter a decline)."},"468":{"id":"/meetings-24","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#start-a-recording","content":"Let the other people know you're recording. If the speech model isn't on your\nMac yet, your first meeting downloads it; the audio is recorded either way."},"469":{"id":"/meetings-25","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"In **Settings → Meetings**:"},"470":{"id":"/meetings-26","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"Setting"},"471":{"id":"/meetings-27","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"What it does"},"472":{"id":"/meetings-28","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Microphone**"},"473":{"id":"/meetings-29","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"Pick the input, and use **Test input** to check it."},"474":{"id":"/meetings-30","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Meeting hotkey**"},"475":{"id":"/meetings-31","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"Change ⇧⌘M."},"476":{"id":"/meetings-32","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Audio sources**"},"477":{"id":"/meetings-33","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Microphone + System Audio** (default) records your voice and the call together, as separate time-aligned tracks. **System Audio Only** records just what's playing on your Mac."},"478":{"id":"/meetings-34","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Live speaker labels**"},"479":{"id":"/meetings-35","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"On by default: speakers are labeled as you talk. When it's off, live captions say *Me* and *Others*, and speakers are separated after the call."},"480":{"id":"/meetings-36","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Double-check speakers by voice**"},"481":{"id":"/meetings-37","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"Off by default; appears while live labels are on. A second on-device check of the live labels."},"482":{"id":"/meetings-38","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Playback mix**"},"483":{"id":"/meetings-39","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**Stereo** (default; your voice and the call on separate channels) or **Mono** (one blended channel, smaller)."},"484":{"id":"/meetings-40","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"**System audio route**"},"485":{"id":"/meetings-41","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"Whether meetings hear the call through System Audio Recording (lighter) or through screen capture, with **Allow now** or **Check again**."},"486":{"id":"/meetings-42","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#audio-and-meeting-settings","content":"A Mac with no microphone records system audio only. Switching speakers or\nheadphones during a meeting, Bluetooth included, doesn't lose the recording."},"487":{"id":"/meetings-43","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"Click the floating pill to open the meeting panel. There are no tabs: your\nnotes are on the left and the live transcript is on the right."},"488":{"id":"/meetings-44","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"**The top row** shows **RECORDING** or **PAUSED**, the elapsed time and a live\nwaveform (it reads **ROOM QUIET** when nobody is talking). On the right: **Mute\nmic** (Microphone + System Audio only), **Pause** / **Resume**, and **Stop\nrecording**. Pausing leaves no gap: the saved audio plays back seamlessly."},"489":{"id":"/meetings-45","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"**Notes.** Type as the meeting runs; your notes save as you go. The flag button\n(for example **Add 3:42**, showing the current time) stamps the recording time\ninto your notes."},"490":{"id":"/meetings-46","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"**As we go.** Below your notes, the As we go digest keeps track of topics (with\nminute marks), decisions, open questions and next steps. It first appears\nafter about two minutes of conversation and refreshes at most every three\nminutes. It needs an AI provider and pauses while your Mac is saving power."},"491":{"id":"/meetings-47","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"**Related.** When a meeting starts, a quiet line under your notes can show\n**1 related** or **3 related**: past moments, meetings or files that match\nthis one. Only the count shows, since the panel is often shared on screen;\nclick it to see the titles, or ✕ to hide them for this meeting. Turn it off\nwith **Show related moments** in **Settings → Speech**."},"492":{"id":"/meetings-48","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"**Live Transcript.** Captions appear a few seconds after people speak. When the\npanel is narrow, the transcript moves to a bar along the bottom. When several\npeople share your Mac's own microphone, the live transcript shows them all as\n*Me*; the saved transcript separates them."},"493":{"id":"/meetings-49","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-live-panel","content":"**Discard.** The trash icon next to **Stop recording** asks &#x2A;Discard\nRecording?* before throwing away everything captured so far."},"494":{"id":"/meetings-50","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#ask-during-a-meeting","content":"At the foot of the live transcript, type in &#x2A;*Ask about what's been said…** to\nask your AI provider about the conversation so far and your notes. Without a\nprovider you'll see *Ask needs an AI provider* and an **Open Settings** button.\nThe conversation carries over to the saved meeting's **Ask** tab."},"495":{"id":"/meetings-51","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-floating-pill","content":"While a meeting is active, a small pill floats on top of every app."},"496":{"id":"/meetings-52","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-floating-pill","content":"**Hover** to show Pause and a separate Stop button."},"497":{"id":"/meetings-53","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-floating-pill","content":"**Click** to open the panel while recording; after you stop, a click shows\nthe transcription progress or opens the saved meeting."},"498":{"id":"/meetings-54","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-floating-pill","content":"**Right-click** for **Stop**, **Pause** / **Resume**, **Open** and\n&#x2A;*Cancel…** (Cancel asks before deleting the recording). After the meeting is\nsaved, right-click offers **Open Meeting** and **Dismiss**."},"499":{"id":"/meetings-55","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#after-a-meeting","content":"When you press **Stop recording**, Everpaper finishes transcribing on your Mac\nand saves the meeting to **Recent meetings** on the Meetings page."},"500":{"id":"/meetings-56","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#after-a-meeting","content":"A recording stopped within its first five seconds isn't kept (&#x2A;That wasn't long\nenough to keep.*). If Everpaper quits or your Mac restarts mid-meeting, the\naudio isn't lost: the Meetings page lists it under **Needs attention**, marked\n*Stopped mid-recording*, with a **Recover** button. Recovery re-transcribes the\nwhole recording and can take several minutes."},"501":{"id":"/meetings-57","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#after-a-meeting","content":"A saved meeting opens on four tabs: **Transcript** (⌘1),\n**Overview** (⌘2, with the summary and templates), **Ask**\n(⌘3, to keep asking about the meeting) and **Speakers**\n(⌘4). The toolbar has **Copy**, **Export** (Plain Text, Markdown,\nSRT subtitles, WebVTT or JSON), **Audio** (saves the recording as an .m4a file)\nand **More** (to-dos, re-analysis, &#x2A;*Rename…**, **Name from Calendar Event**).\nPress ⌘F to find words in the transcript. In the Library, each row\nalso has &#x2A;*Save Transcript…** and &#x2A;*Save Audio…**."},"502":{"id":"/meetings-58","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#after-a-meeting","content":"To bring in a transcript from another tool, click &#x2A;*Import Transcript…** on the\nMeetings page and choose a WebVTT (.vtt) file; no audio is needed."},"503":{"id":"/meetings-59","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#everyday-or-detailed","content":"Choose how meetings are transcribed in **Settings → Speech → Meetings**.\n**Everyday** (the default) is fast: live captions and speaker labels as you\ntalk. **Detailed** re-listens to the whole call after you stop, so results take\nlonger but are more thorough; it needs a one-time download of about 2 GB. If\nyou pick Detailed before it's set up, meetings use Everyday until it is."},"504":{"id":"/meetings-60","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#everyday-or-detailed","content":"To redo one meeting, open it and choose **More → Re-analyze Audio**,\n&#x2A;*Re-analyze with the Detailed model (slower)**, or &#x2A;*Re-analyze with…** to\npick a model."},"505":{"id":"/meetings-61","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#the-automatic-summary","content":"When an AI provider is set up, each finished meeting gets a **Summary** card,\nmarked *Automatic*, on its Overview tab. Everpaper writes one for meetings from\nthe last 7 days with more than a few minutes of talk (about 4,000 characters of\ntranscript), and for any older meeting when you open it. It waits about half a\nminute for speaker names and the title to settle, and never runs while you're\nrecording. Once it's there, it replaces the As we go digest. A local provider\nkeeps it on your Mac. With a cloud provider, it waits until you turn on\n**Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** in **Settings → AI & summaries**."},"506":{"id":"/meetings-62","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#templates-and-marked-prompts","content":"On the **Overview** tab, **Generate** runs a template on the meeting: **Open\nThreads**, **Commitment Register**, **Decision Rationale**, **Meeting Memo**,\n**Risk Review**, **Follow-Up Letter** or **Perspective Matrix**."},"507":{"id":"/meetings-63","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#templates-and-marked-prompts","content":"On the Meetings page, the **After each meeting** card has the switch &#x2A;*Run\nmarked prompts automatically (sends the transcript to your AI provider)**. It's\noff by default. When it's on, every template marked Auto-run runs as soon as a\nmeeting finishes; **Meeting Memo** is marked out of the box. Use &#x2A;*Edit\nPrompts…** to add prompts, to pin, hide or mark them, or to reset the\nbuilt-ins."},"508":{"id":"/meetings-64","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#speaker-names","content":"On a saved meeting's **Speakers** tab, click **Name this speaker** to name a\nvoice, or **Forget name** to undo. Everpaper fills in some names itself, and\nsays where each came from:"},"509":{"id":"/meetings-65","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#speaker-names","content":"**from the calendar invite**: a one-to-one call whose invite lists exactly\none guest."},"510":{"id":"/meetings-66","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#speaker-names","content":"**recognised from an earlier meeting**: a voice you named before."},"511":{"id":"/meetings-67","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#speaker-names","content":"Everpaper remembers a voice only after it has a name. To stop it, turn off\n**Remember voices between meetings** in **Settings → Privacy → Voices, storage\n& journal controls**; that deletes every stored voice. If two labels are the\nsame person, the merge card asks whether **They're the same person**."},"512":{"id":"/meetings-68","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#hiding-speakers","content":"**Hide my voice from this transcript**: a link at the top of the transcript\nremoves your turns from view; **Show my voice** brings them back."},"513":{"id":"/meetings-69","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#hiding-speakers","content":"**Hide from transcript**: on the **Speakers** tab, hide any speaker. Hidden\nspeakers appear in a **Hidden** section with **Unhide** and **Unhide all**."},"514":{"id":"/meetings-70","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#hiding-speakers","content":"Hiding survives re-analysis. It changes only what this meeting's transcript\nshows: **Copy**, **Export**, **Audio** and the meeting's Summary still include\neveryone. To remove a recording, delete the meeting."},"515":{"id":"/meetings-71","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#to-dos-from-a-meeting","content":"With an AI provider set up, **Today's focus** on the Today page picks up action\nitems from your recent meetings by itself. To pull them from one meeting\nyourself, for example after fixing the transcript, open it and choose **More →\nExtract To-Dos into Today**. Each to-do is labeled with the meeting it came\nfrom."},"516":{"id":"/meetings-72","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#privacy","content":"Recording and transcription run entirely on your Mac, and recordings are never\nuploaded. AI features (live Ask, the As we go digest, the automatic Summary,\ntemplates, marked prompts and to-do extraction) use the AI provider you set\nup. A provider on your Mac keeps everything local. A cloud provider receives\nmeeting text only after you turn on **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal**\nin **Settings → AI & summaries**. Before anything is sent, secrets such as API\nkeys and card numbers are removed, and email addresses, phone numbers and names\nit detects are replaced. See AI on your Mac."},"517":{"id":"/meetings-73","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#privacy","content":"On macOS 27, meetings are also indexed on this Mac by what was heard in them,\nso you can find one by its sound as well as its words. See\nSearch by meaning."},"518":{"id":"/meetings-74","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#privacy","content":"Recording laws differ by place. Tell people when you're recording them."},"519":{"id":"/meetings-75","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#related-reading","content":"Transcribe meetings in 25 European languages: which languages the speech model covers."},"520":{"id":"/meetings-76","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#related-reading","content":"Best AI meeting assistants: how bot and bot-free tools compare."},"521":{"id":"/meetings-77","page_id":"/meetings","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/meetings#related-reading","content":"Who hears your meetings: where meeting audio goes."},"522":{"id":"/privacy","page_id":"/privacy","type":"page","content":"Privacy","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy"},"523":{"id":"/privacy-0","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy","content":"How Everpaper keeps your data on-device by default, how optional cloud AI is gated by consent and redacted before it leaves your Mac, and where to configure a provider and keys."},"524":{"id":"/privacy-1","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#on-device-by-default","content":"On-device by default"},"525":{"id":"/privacy-2","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#what-connects-to-the-internet","content":"What connects to the internet"},"526":{"id":"/privacy-3","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#how-long-its-kept","content":"How long it's kept"},"527":{"id":"/privacy-4","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"AI is opt-in"},"528":{"id":"/privacy-5","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Secrets are removed before any AI call"},"529":{"id":"/privacy-6","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"Computer History"},"530":{"id":"/privacy-7","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#keeping-apps-and-sites-out","content":"Keeping apps and sites out"},"531":{"id":"/privacy-8","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Choices and their defaults"},"532":{"id":"/privacy-9","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#local-ai-sees-the-real-thing","content":"Local AI sees the real thing"},"533":{"id":"/privacy-10","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#answers-are-checked","content":"Answers are checked"},"534":{"id":"/privacy-11","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"Deleting what Everpaper keeps"},"535":{"id":"/privacy-12","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"Where to configure it"},"536":{"id":"/privacy-13","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#where-your-keys-are-stored","content":"Where your keys are stored"},"537":{"id":"/privacy-14","page_id":"/privacy","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/privacy#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"538":{"id":"/privacy-15","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy","content":"Everpaper is built to stay on your Mac. Capture, transcription, the knowledge\ngraph, and your whole journal database live locally, and nothing is sent to an AI\nunless you connect a provider and — for cloud providers — explicitly turn cloud\nanalysis on. This page explains exactly what stays put, what can leave, and how\nto control it."},"539":{"id":"/privacy-16","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#on-device-by-default","content":"Out of the box, everything happens on your machine:"},"540":{"id":"/privacy-17","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#on-device-by-default","content":"**Screen capture and text recognition.** In the screen history modes,\nEverpaper takes screenshots of your displays and reads them on this Mac.\nScreenshots are stored locally and never uploaded."},"541":{"id":"/privacy-18","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#on-device-by-default","content":"**Meeting transcription.** Meetings are recorded and transcribed by\non-device speech models. Recordings are never uploaded."},"542":{"id":"/privacy-19","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#on-device-by-default","content":"**Your journal and graph.** The journal database, the people, files, sites,\nand beliefs in Memory (also called Second Brain), and your meeting library\nare all stored on this Mac."},"543":{"id":"/privacy-20","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#on-device-by-default","content":"**Insights, Connections and beliefs** in Memory are worked out on this Mac\nfrom your own history, so they work with no AI provider connected at all."},"544":{"id":"/privacy-21","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#what-connects-to-the-internet","content":"Everpaper goes online only for these:"},"545":{"id":"/privacy-22","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#what-connects-to-the-internet","content":"**Model downloads**, when you set up speech or AI models (for example with\n**Prepare on this Mac** or **Set up**), or when your first meeting needs the\ntranscription model: from Hugging Face and everpaper.app, and the oMLX server\nfrom GitHub. After setup, the search model also downloads by itself at a\nquiet moment, unless you postponed it or chose &#x2A;*Apple (previous)** under\n**Search model**; see Search by meaning."},"546":{"id":"/privacy-23","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#what-connects-to-the-internet","content":"**Update checks** to everpaper.app, daily by default and never while a\nmeeting is recording. Choose how they work, or turn them off, in **Settings →\nGeneral → Updates**."},"547":{"id":"/privacy-24","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#what-connects-to-the-internet","content":"**Your AI provider**, and an **External embeddings provider** if you set\none, under the rules below. Search by meaning runs on this Mac and sends\nnothing."},"548":{"id":"/privacy-25","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#what-connects-to-the-internet","content":"Nothing else. Everpaper has no analytics or telemetry. Recordings, screenshots\nand your calendar are never uploaded. Only text, such as screen text,\ntranscripts and meeting titles, can reach an AI you set up. The Everpaper\nbrowser extension talks only to Everpaper on this Mac."},"549":{"id":"/privacy-26","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#how-long-its-kept","content":"Screenshots are deleted after **30 days** by default (**Settings → Privacy →\nKeep screenshot images for**: 7, 30, 90 days or Forever). The same choice is\nalso in **Settings → Daily history → How long it stays**, as **Keep\nscreenshots for**."},"550":{"id":"/privacy-27","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#how-long-its-kept","content":"On a new install, **Also delete expired text & recall data** (under &#x2A;*Manage\nsaved text…**) is on. In Daily history the same switch is called **Also delete\ntheir text & recall data**. After the same period, Everpaper also deletes that\nday's recognized text, search data, running notes and written entry. Some of\nthe day, such as the app timeline and the notes you typed yourself, can stay;\nto remove everything, delete the day. Turn the switch off to keep text and\nentries after the images go. If you upgraded from a build that already had\njournal data, it starts off and only images are deleted."},"551":{"id":"/privacy-28","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#how-long-its-kept","content":"Original typed text from Computer History expires after 48 hours. Meeting\nrecordings are kept until you delete them."},"552":{"id":"/privacy-29","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"Everpaper never talks to an AI provider unless you set one up:"},"553":{"id":"/privacy-30","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"**No provider, no traffic.** If you haven't configured a provider, features\nthat use AI (answers in &#x2A;*Ask your memory…** and Memory's **Ask** tab,\nsummaries) simply wait. Nothing is sent to any AI."},"554":{"id":"/privacy-31","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"**On-device providers keep everything on your Mac**: Everpaper Native, or\nOllama, LM Studio, oMLX or Nativ while their address is on this Mac, which is\nthe default. If you point one of them at another computer, Everpaper treats it\nlike a cloud provider. For an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, you decide with\n**This is a trusted, private endpoint**. Trusted endpoints receive text\nwithout the cloud switch, with only secrets removed, so turn it on only for a\nserver you control."},"555":{"id":"/privacy-32","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"**Cloud providers are gated by consent.** A cloud provider (Anthropic, OpenAI,\nGoogle Gemini, OpenRouter) is only allowed to receive your data after you turn\non **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal**, which is **off by default**."},"556":{"id":"/privacy-33","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"**Meeting summaries.** Recording and transcription stay on your Mac. If you\nset up AI, the transcript of each recent meeting goes to your AI to write its\n**Summary**. With a cloud provider, this happens only after you turn on\n**Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal**. **Run marked prompts\nautomatically** (Meetings page, off by default) also sends transcripts after\neach meeting."},"557":{"id":"/privacy-34","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#ai-is-opt-in","content":"Every AI feature in the app passes the same check before anything is sent: if\nno provider is configured the call is declined, an on-device or trusted\nprovider is allowed, and a cloud provider is allowed only with your consent.\nJournal text, meeting transcripts, chat questions and notes all go through it.\nTwo things work differently: &#x2A;*Allow external agents (MCP)** lets another AI\napp read your journal (see below), and the\ncommand line's AI commands send text to the provider you name on each call\n(see Command line). See\nAI on your Mac for every option."},"558":{"id":"/privacy-35","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Before any text is sent to a provider, Everpaper runs an offline,\non-device pass that scrubs secrets out of it. This runs both at capture time\n(before anything is written to your journal) and again before every outbound AI\ncall. It recognizes:"},"559":{"id":"/privacy-36","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Private keys"},"560":{"id":"/privacy-37","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"JSON Web Tokens (JWTs)"},"561":{"id":"/privacy-38","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"API keys"},"562":{"id":"/privacy-39","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Bearer tokens"},"563":{"id":"/privacy-40","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Payment card numbers"},"564":{"id":"/privacy-41","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Social Security numbers"},"565":{"id":"/privacy-42","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"One-time passcodes (OTPs)"},"566":{"id":"/privacy-43","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"For cloud providers, and endpoints you haven't marked trusted, Everpaper also\nreplaces email addresses, phone numbers and names it detects, for example\n`[REDACTED:email]`."},"567":{"id":"/privacy-44","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#secrets-are-removed-before-any-ai-call","content":"Each match is replaced inline with a placeholder like `[REDACTED:api_key]`\nbefore the text is saved or sent to an AI. Screenshots are images, so a secret\nthat was on screen still shows in them, and only patterns like those above are\ncaught. The redaction pass runs entirely on your Mac and makes no network calls\nof its own."},"568":{"id":"/privacy-45","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"Computer History is an optional record of what you do on your Mac, beyond\nwhat's on screen. It's offered in every history mode except Screen history, and\nstays off until you turn it on (**Computer History events & text** in setup,\n**Record clicks and text** in **Settings → Daily history**)."},"569":{"id":"/privacy-46","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**What it records.** Clicks, shortcuts, text you select (**Text you select**)\nand text you type (**Text you type**), in all apps and websites unless you\nexclude them. This can include email and messages. You can turn selected or\ntyped text off on its own."},"570":{"id":"/privacy-47","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**What it never records.** Password fields and private browsing."},"571":{"id":"/privacy-48","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**How typed text is kept.** As an encrypted, redacted record. The key is kept\nin this Mac's Keychain and doesn't sync. The original text is gone after 48\nhours."},"572":{"id":"/privacy-49","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**Permissions.** **Accessibility**, to read the controls and text you chose,\nand **Input Monitoring**, to notice clicks and shortcuts. Grant them in setup\nor in **Settings → Daily history → Set up permissions**."},"573":{"id":"/privacy-50","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**Limiting it.** &#x2A;*Settings → Daily history → Interaction source policy →\nManage…** sets the default for apps and websites: **Observe unless excluded**\nor **Only included sources**, plus rules per app and per website. For\nper-website rules in Safari, turn on the **Everpaper Browser Bridge** extension\n(**Safari setup** in the same sheet; pair with a code valid for five minutes).\nIt sends only the current site's address and whether the window is private,\nand only to Everpaper on this Mac. **Revoke all** removes every pairing."},"574":{"id":"/privacy-51","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**Other people.** Communication apps are included unless you exclude or pause\nthem. Capture other people's communications only with their prior consent."},"575":{"id":"/privacy-52","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#computer-history","content":"**What your AI sees.** While it's kept, the text you select and type is part of\nwhat your AI reads to write the day's running notes and entry, and those can\nquote or summarize it. They stay after the 48 hours, under\nHow long it's kept; delete the day to remove them. It is\nstored only on this Mac. A cloud AI receives it only after you turn on **Allow\ncloud AI to analyze your journal**; a trusted endpoint receives it without that\nswitch."},"576":{"id":"/privacy-53","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#keeping-apps-and-sites-out","content":"Screenshots are opt-out: everything can be captured except what you tell\nEverpaper to skip. Three choices in **Settings → Privacy → What gets saved**\napply to the timed screenshots and to Detailed screen history's extra images\nalike:"},"577":{"id":"/privacy-54","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#keeping-apps-and-sites-out","content":"**Skip apps**: apps Everpaper never captures while they are in front. No\napps are skipped until you add them."},"578":{"id":"/privacy-55","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#keeping-apps-and-sites-out","content":"**Skip sites**: websites to keep out of screenshots while they're in front.\nSubdomains count too: skipping example.com also skips mail.example.com.\nType an address, or tap a suggestion (common email, chat and messaging\nsites). Nothing is skipped until you add it. Email and chat aren't left out\non their own, so add them here if you want them kept out."},"579":{"id":"/privacy-56","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#keeping-apps-and-sites-out","content":"**Skip private browsing windows**, on by default: while a private or\nincognito window is in front, Everpaper takes no screenshot and keeps no\nwindow title. With the Everpaper browser extension it uses the browser's\nown private-window state; without it, it looks for the marker browsers put\nin the window title. Detection is best effort, and a private window it\ncan't recognize is treated as a normal one, so add sensitive sites to\n**Skip sites** as well."},"580":{"id":"/privacy-57","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#keeping-apps-and-sites-out","content":"Detailed screen history takes its window images in browsers with or without\nthe extension, reading the page address through Accessibility, and still\nleaves out skipped sites and private windows. A screenshot\nshows your whole display, so a skipped app, site or private window that is\nvisible behind another window can still appear. Use\n**Pause**, or Activity only, for sensitive\nwork. The related moments on Today and in meetings never start from a skipped\napp, a skipped site or a private window. For Computer History, use\n&#x2A;*Interaction source policy → Manage…** to exclude apps and websites."},"581":{"id":"/privacy-58","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"All of these are in **Settings** unless noted."},"582":{"id":"/privacy-59","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Choice"},"583":{"id":"/privacy-60","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Default"},"584":{"id":"/privacy-61","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Where"},"585":{"id":"/privacy-62","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal**"},"586":{"id":"/privacy-63","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off"},"587":{"id":"/privacy-64","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"AI & summaries → Your memory & summaries (and Privacy)"},"588":{"id":"/privacy-65","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Share your profile with cloud AI**"},"589":{"id":"/privacy-66","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off"},"590":{"id":"/privacy-67","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"under the switch above"},"591":{"id":"/privacy-68","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Run marked prompts automatically**"},"592":{"id":"/privacy-69","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off"},"593":{"id":"/privacy-70","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Meetings** page → After each meeting"},"594":{"id":"/privacy-71","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Allow external agents (MCP)**"},"595":{"id":"/privacy-72","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off"},"596":{"id":"/privacy-73","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"AI & summaries → Access from other AI apps"},"597":{"id":"/privacy-74","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"…including raw screen text (full-text search)"},"598":{"id":"/privacy-75","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off; revoked when MCP is turned off"},"599":{"id":"/privacy-76","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"same place"},"600":{"id":"/privacy-77","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Computer History (**Record clicks and text**)"},"601":{"id":"/privacy-78","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off"},"602":{"id":"/privacy-79","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Daily history"},"603":{"id":"/privacy-80","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Remember voices between meetings**"},"604":{"id":"/privacy-81","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**on**: a voice is stored only after you name it; &#x2A;*Manage…** forgets one; switching off deletes them all"},"605":{"id":"/privacy-82","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Privacy → Voices, storage & journal controls"},"606":{"id":"/privacy-83","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**AI refinement of insights**"},"607":{"id":"/privacy-84","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"on when AI is set up"},"608":{"id":"/privacy-85","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"AI & summaries → Your memory & summaries"},"609":{"id":"/privacy-86","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Journal threads**"},"610":{"id":"/privacy-87","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"off"},"611":{"id":"/privacy-88","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"AI & summaries → Your memory & summaries"},"612":{"id":"/privacy-89","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Skip private browsing windows**"},"613":{"id":"/privacy-90","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"on"},"614":{"id":"/privacy-91","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Privacy → What gets saved"},"615":{"id":"/privacy-92","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Skip apps**, **Skip sites**"},"616":{"id":"/privacy-93","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"empty until you add something"},"617":{"id":"/privacy-94","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Privacy → What gets saved"},"618":{"id":"/privacy-95","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Show related moments**"},"619":{"id":"/privacy-96","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"on"},"620":{"id":"/privacy-97","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"Speech"},"621":{"id":"/privacy-98","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"**Search model**"},"622":{"id":"/privacy-99","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"EmbeddingGemma-2, on this Mac"},"623":{"id":"/privacy-100","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"AI & summaries → Files you include"},"624":{"id":"/privacy-101","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#choices-and-their-defaults","content":"External agents get people, files, links and connections, with secrets removed\n(names, email addresses and phone numbers are kept), and never screenshots.\nWhat an agent reads is then handled by that app and the AI it uses, which may\nbe a cloud service. **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** doesn't apply to\nit, so turn MCP on only for apps you trust. **AI refinement of insights** lets\nyour AI tidy the beliefs and topics in Memory; turn it off to keep the plain\nversion. Like everything else, it uses only the AI you chose, under the same\nrules."},"625":{"id":"/privacy-102","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#local-ai-sees-the-real-thing","content":"When you use a private provider (Everpaper Native; Ollama, LM Studio, oMLX or\nNativ on this Mac; or an endpoint you marked trusted), Everpaper sends the\nfull, un-redacted context. It preserves real names, emails, and phone numbers\nso Memory grounds on the real thing instead of `[REDACTED:name]` placeholders.\nOn-device providers keep all of it on your Mac. A trusted endpoint receives it\nas is, which is why you should mark only a server you control. Secrets (cards,\nkeys, tokens) are still scrubbed for every provider, local or cloud."},"626":{"id":"/privacy-103","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#answers-are-checked","content":"Before a Memory answer is shown, Everpaper checks each sentence. If it names a\nperson, file or other named thing that isn't in your captured history, or cites\na source that doesn't exist, that sentence is removed. A name that is only a\nclose match is kept but flagged. This catches most invented names, but it can't\njudge every fact, so open the cited sources before you rely on an answer."},"627":{"id":"/privacy-104","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"**One day**: on its page in **Timeline**, **Delete this day and all its\nevidence**. You can undo it from Today right after."},"628":{"id":"/privacy-105","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"**One meeting**: in **Meetings**, right-click it and choose **Delete**. Its\naudio goes too, and this can't be undone."},"629":{"id":"/privacy-106","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"**All meetings**: **Settings → General → Setup & data → Clear meeting\nhistory** (type DELETE to confirm). &#x2A;*Settings → Privacy → Delete saved\nhistory…** takes you there."},"630":{"id":"/privacy-107","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"**Voices**: forget one in **Remembered voices** (&#x2A;*Manage…**), or all of them\nby turning off **Remember voices between meetings**."},"631":{"id":"/privacy-108","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"**Downloaded models**: speech models under **Settings → Speech → Models on\nthis Mac → Remove**; Everpaper Native models under **Settings → AI &\nsummaries → AI connection → Remove**."},"632":{"id":"/privacy-109","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#deleting-what-everpaper-keeps","content":"Your journal and meetings are stored in Everpaper's folder in your user\nLibrary. Some downloaded models are kept elsewhere, so remove models with the\nbuttons above rather than by deleting folders."},"633":{"id":"/privacy-110","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"Open **Settings** (sidebar, or ⌘,). AI choices are in **AI &\nsummaries → AI connection**. What is saved, for how long, and what is shared\nare in **Privacy**."},"634":{"id":"/privacy-111","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"To connect a provider:"},"635":{"id":"/privacy-112","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"Pick a provider from **AI option** (or **None** to disconnect)."},"636":{"id":"/privacy-113","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"For a cloud provider, paste your **API key**. For a local provider, you can\nusually leave the key blank."},"637":{"id":"/privacy-114","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"Optionally set a **base URL** (for OpenAI-compatible endpoints this is\nrequired) and a **model**, or use **Refresh list** to pull available models."},"638":{"id":"/privacy-115","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"Press **Save**, then **Test Connection**."},"639":{"id":"/privacy-116","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-to-configure-it","content":"With a cloud provider, **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** appears under\n**Your memory & summaries**. It is off by default and is also in Privacy as\n**Allow online journal analysis**. Turn it on, and **Share your profile with\ncloud AI** appears beneath it; it sends your name, role and what you wrote\nabout yourself. With only on-device or trusted providers, the page instead\nsays &#x2A;Your AI uses only on-device or trusted private providers — cloud AI is\noff.* The MCP switches are under **Access from other AI apps**."},"640":{"id":"/privacy-117","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#where-your-keys-are-stored","content":"Your API key is stored only in the **macOS Keychain**, in a per-provider entry\nunder an Everpaper-specific service. It is never written to the app's\npreferences and never appears in your saved configuration. Switching providers\nkeeps each provider's key in the Keychain, so you can move back and forth without\nre-entering it. **Clear** disconnects the current AI and removes its key from\nthe Keychain. To change a key, paste the new one and press **Save**."},"641":{"id":"/privacy-118","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#related-reading","content":"What leaves your Mac: how the data path compares with other memory and meeting apps."},"642":{"id":"/privacy-119","page_id":"/privacy","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/privacy#related-reading","content":"Who hears your meetings: where audio goes with bot-based and cloud notetakers."},"643":{"id":"/recall","page_id":"/recall","type":"page","content":"Recall","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall"},"644":{"id":"/recall-0","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall","content":"Ask your book a question and get an answer drawn from your own days, meetings and files, found by what they mean, with a link back to the exact moment it came from."},"645":{"id":"/recall-1","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#the-concordance-from-any-app","content":"The Concordance: from any app"},"646":{"id":"/recall-2","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"The Index: jump anywhere"},"647":{"id":"/recall-3","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#ask-your-memory-a-question-across-every-day","content":"Ask your memory: a question across every day"},"648":{"id":"/recall-4","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#how-the-answer-is-built","content":"How the answer is built"},"649":{"id":"/recall-5","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"Quick filters"},"650":{"id":"/recall-6","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#what-you-keep-coming-back-to","content":"What you keep coming back to"},"651":{"id":"/recall-7","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#search-by-meaning","content":"Search by meaning"},"652":{"id":"/recall-8","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#setting-it-up","content":"Setting it up"},"653":{"id":"/recall-9","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#asking-about-a-single-meeting","content":"Asking about a single meeting"},"654":{"id":"/recall-10","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#a-note-on-where-this-runs","content":"A note on where this runs"},"655":{"id":"/recall-11","page_id":"/recall","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/recall#related-reading","content":"Related reading"},"656":{"id":"/recall-12","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall","content":"Recall is how you ask your book a question and get a real answer back — built\nfrom what you actually saw and recorded, not from the open web. You can ask\nfrom four places. **The Concordance** (⌥Space, from any app) finds\nor asks across days, meetings and indexed files. **The Index** (⌘K)\njumps to a page. &#x2A;*Ask your memory…** on Today searches anything you saw.\n**Memory → Ask** (⌥⌘1) is for longer conversations. Single days and\nmeetings have their own Ask fields."},"657":{"id":"/recall-13","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-concordance-from-any-app","content":"Press ⌥Space in any app to open the Concordance, a small floating\npanel. Choose **Find** to jump to a day, a meeting or an indexed file, or\n**Ask** to get an answer about anything you've captured. Narrow it with\n**All**, **Days**, **Meetings** or **Files** (⌘1–⌘4)."},"658":{"id":"/recall-14","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-concordance-from-any-app","content":"In **Files**, and the file rows in **All**, files whose names or text match\nappear at once; files that match what you meant follow a moment later. What\nyou type in the Concordance is searched on this Mac only."},"659":{"id":"/recall-15","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-concordance-from-any-app","content":"After an answer, **Correct** sets the record straight for future answers, and\n**Continue in Memory** (⌘Return) carries the conversation into\nMemory's Ask tab."},"660":{"id":"/recall-16","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-concordance-from-any-app","content":"Change the shortcut in **Settings → General → The Concordance**. If another\napp has taken it, use **Go → Summon the Concordance**."},"661":{"id":"/recall-17","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"Press ⌘K anywhere in Everpaper to open the Index. It is both a\ntable of contents and a search box for the whole book."},"662":{"id":"/recall-18","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"Start typing and it filters across everything in one place:"},"663":{"id":"/recall-19","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"**The Days**: any finished day, by title, summary, or date."},"664":{"id":"/recall-20","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"**Meetings**: a recorded meeting, by title."},"665":{"id":"/recall-21","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"**Commonplace Book**: beliefs Memory has formed."},"666":{"id":"/recall-22","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"**Lexicon**: your word corrections and saved phrases."},"667":{"id":"/recall-23","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"**Settings**: any setting, landing on its own row."},"668":{"id":"/recall-24","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"**Commands**: actions such as Turn to today, Begin meeting / End meeting,\nRun setup again, Check for updates."},"669":{"id":"/recall-25","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"Open with an empty query and the Index shows a table of contents instead: the\nParts of your book (Today, Meetings, Timeline, Library, Memory, Settings), your\nthree most recent days and meetings, and common commands."},"670":{"id":"/recall-26","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#the-index-jump-anywhere","content":"Move the selection with the up and down arrows, press Return to go,\nand Esc to dismiss — focus returns to the page you were on."},"671":{"id":"/recall-27","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#ask-your-memory-a-question-across-every-day","content":"When you want an answer rather than a destination, ask the book. On **Today**,\ntype in &#x2A;*Ask your memory…** (or choose **Go → Ask the Book**,\n⇧⌘A, to jump there), or try a chip such as &#x2A;What did I decide?*. In **Timeline**, **Ask the\nbook** (⌘F) opens the same search across every day."},"672":{"id":"/recall-28","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#ask-your-memory-a-question-across-every-day","content":"The search view, headed **Ask the book**, looks through **anything you saw,\nacross every day**. Type a question — \"what was the address jane.smith sent\nme?\", \"which build broke last Thursday?\" — and the book answers from your own\ncaptured history."},"673":{"id":"/recall-29","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#how-the-answer-is-built","content":"If Everpaper may use your AI (an on-device or trusted private provider, or a\ncloud provider with **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** turned on), the\nanswer streams back as prose, written only from the days and frames that match\nyour question. Under the answer is a **Sources** list. Each source is the exact\nframe the answer drew from, shown as its time, the app, and the window title —\nfor example:"},"674":{"id":"/recall-30","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#how-the-answer-is-built","content":"Click any source to open that frame: the original screen, at the moment it was\ncaptured, so you can verify the answer with your own eyes. Every `[#N]` in the\nanswer maps to a row in the list. Answers can still get a detail wrong, so open\nthe sources when it matters."},"675":{"id":"/recall-31","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#how-the-answer-is-built","content":"If Everpaper can't use an AI for this, Recall still works. Instead of prose, it\nreturns **cards** — each one a specific match (a phone number, an email, a\nlink, a file you saw) carrying the same time-and-place stamp, and a click opens\nthe frame it came from. Recording and search never need AI; the answer style\njust changes."},"676":{"id":"/recall-32","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"The **Ask the book** view offers chips you can click for the things people\nlook for most:"},"677":{"id":"/recall-33","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"**Phone numbers**"},"678":{"id":"/recall-34","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"**Emails**"},"679":{"id":"/recall-35","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"**Links**"},"680":{"id":"/recall-36","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"**Files**"},"681":{"id":"/recall-37","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#quick-filters","content":"Click one to seed the search and see every matching moment."},"682":{"id":"/recall-38","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#what-you-keep-coming-back-to","content":"Before you've typed anything, Recall shows **You keep coming back to** — the\npeople, sites, and files that recur across your days, each with how many days\nit spans and how many times you've seen it. Click one to turn it into a search."},"683":{"id":"/recall-39","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#search-by-meaning","content":"Everpaper searches your days, meetings and files with a search model that runs\non this Mac, **EmbeddingGemma-2**. It finds a moment by what it was about, even\nwhen you describe it in other words, or in another language, than the ones on\nscreen. Exact names and phrases still match first. It's what Ask the book,\n&#x2A;*Ask your memory…**, the Concordance and Memory's **Ask** use to find their\nsources."},"684":{"id":"/recall-40","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#search-by-meaning","content":"On macOS 27 it goes further:"},"685":{"id":"/recall-41","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#search-by-meaning","content":"**Screenshots, by what they show.** Describe a picture, a chart or a design,\nand Everpaper can find the screenshot even when it has no readable text."},"686":{"id":"/recall-42","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#search-by-meaning","content":"**Meetings, by what was heard.** A meeting can be found by its sound, not\nonly its transcript, and the answer can say where in the recording it was\nheard. Its source opens the matching part of the transcript."},"687":{"id":"/recall-43","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#search-by-meaning","content":"Before macOS 27, search by meaning covers text; screenshots and meetings stay\nsearchable by their words."},"688":{"id":"/recall-44","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#setting-it-up","content":"The search model is a one-time download, about 1.5 GB on macOS 27 and less on\nearlier macOS, then a few minutes of preparation on this Mac. You can prepare\nit in setup with **Prepare on this Mac**. If you already use Everpaper, a\n**NEW IN THIS IMPRESSION** card, **Search that finds what you mean**, offers\n**Set it up** or **Not now**. Otherwise it sets itself up in the background at a quiet moment; **Not\nnow**, **Set up later** or cancelling puts that off for a week."},"689":{"id":"/recall-45","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#setting-it-up","content":"Search keeps working the old way until the model is ready, and your older\nhistory is brought up to date gradually in the background, which can take a\nwhile on a large library. Preparation runs again, for a few minutes, after a\nmacOS update."},"690":{"id":"/recall-46","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#setting-it-up","content":"To go back to the previous search, choose &#x2A;*Apple (previous)** under **Search\nmodel** in **Settings → AI & summaries → Files you include**. Nothing is lost,\nand you can switch back at any time. With Apple chosen, the search model\ndoesn't download."},"691":{"id":"/recall-47","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#asking-about-a-single-meeting","content":"Open the meeting, choose the **Ask** tab and type in &#x2A;*Ask this meeting…**.\nWhile a meeting is still recording, use &#x2A;*Ask about what’s been said…** under\nthe live transcript. A single finished day has &#x2A;*Ask this day…** at the foot of\nits page."},"692":{"id":"/recall-48","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#a-note-on-where-this-runs","content":"Recall reads your own on-device book. Search and the card results stay\nentirely on your Mac. Search by meaning uses the on-device search model, not\nyour AI provider, so your searches are never sent online to be understood.\nThe one exception is an **External embeddings provider**, an advanced option\nyou would have set yourself: files, and questions asked about them, then also\ngo through it. The Concordance's type-ahead never uses it. See\nFiles and other AI apps.\nThe streamed prose answer uses the AI you set up in\n**Settings → AI & summaries**; an on-device provider keeps that on your Mac\ntoo. See AI on your Mac."},"693":{"id":"/recall-49","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#related-reading","content":"Mac launchers with clipboard history: how this launcher compares with Spotlight, Raycast and Alfred."},"694":{"id":"/recall-50","page_id":"/recall","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/recall#related-reading","content":"Everpaper b101: what the launcher and Dictate do."},"695":{"id":"/release-notes","page_id":"/release-notes","type":"page","content":"Release notes","breadcrumbs":["Release notes"],"tags":["docs"],"url":"/release-notes"},"696":{"id":"/release-notes-0","page_id":"/release-notes","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/release-notes","content":"What changed in each version of Everpaper, newest first."},"697":{"id":"/release-notes-1","page_id":"/release-notes","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"url":"/release-notes#200-b101--beta","content":"2.0.0-b101 — beta"},"698":{"id":"/release-notes-2","page_id":"/release-notes","type":"heading","tags":["docs"],"u