`llm chat` and `prompts run` send the meeting's full transcript and notes to the\nprovider you name. Use a local provider (`ollama`, `lmstudio`, `omlx`, `nativ`)\nto keep them on your Mac."],[1059,"The Colophon learns to answer first: settings you can find, a health check that greets you, and one grammar for every control."],[1075,"The Concordance learns to hold a conversation — and recall gets sharper everywhere it looks."],[645,"The Concordance: from any app"],[116,"The countdown"],[150,"The countdown can only open in the first 30 seconds of the meeting. If your Mac\nwas asleep then, Everpaper won't start recording late, but you'll still get the\nnotification for up to two minutes after the start. If the previous meeting is\nstill being saved, Everpaper keeps trying during those 30 seconds."],[148,"The countdown has no keyboard shortcuts; use the mouse or trackpad."],[149,"The countdown only appears when you're not already recording, and only for\nmeetings you've accepted or tentatively accepted (and your own blocks that have\nno invitation to answer). Meetings you haven't responded to won't auto-record,\nsince recording an unaccepted meeting would be a surprise. You can still get a\nreminder for them."],[900,"The daily journal reads the whole day again."],[18,"The day's running notes and entry (**Day Summary**)"],[1189,"The Days page is also redesigned:"],[235,"The end-of-day review"],[973,"The first build with an engine made only of Apple frameworks — no separate\nAI app required."],[1243,"The first release of Hindsight: a private, on-device daybook for macOS. One\ncontinuous book you turn through page by page, with three pillars and an Index\n(⌘K) that jumps anywhere."],[104,"The first request after the engine starts can take up to about 30 seconds.\nWhen the engine has closed to free memory, the next request waits for it to\nload again."],[360,"The first time you open Everpaper, a welcome page opens, then setup. Setup has\nup to five steps (four if you choose 