ed — not just who and\nwhat kept recurring."],[970,"The setup survives closing the card — an accepted download keeps going in\nthe background."],[393,"The sidebar has six places, and ⌘K opens the Index. See\nFinding your way."],[416,"The sidebar has six places:"],[143,"The stricter choices skip personal blocks and solo focus time. All-day events\nand meetings you've declined are always skipped, whatever you choose."],[1272,"The top of the page shows **Still learning you**, **Getting to know you** or\n**Ready**, and how many active days it has seen. Below that are four counts:\n**Days**, **Frames processed** (screenshots), **Topics** (the distinct people,\nfiles, sites and tickets it has found) and **Recurring threads** (any of these\nseen on more than one day). Click the arrow beside the counts to see the\npercentage and a short note. On the Ask tab, the counts sit behind the chart\nbutton (**Memory details**)."],[323,"The vault covers your days, not your meetings. To export a meeting, open it and\npress **Export** to save its transcript as .txt, .md, .srt, .vtt or .json, or\n**Audio** to save its recording as an .m4a file. Everpaper asks where to save\neach one. In the Library, each row has &#x2A;*Save Transcript…** and &#x2A;*Save Audio…**.\nTo send a meeting's to-dos to Reminders, use **Add to Reminders** in Today's\nfocus. See also Meetings and Command line."],[998,"The wait after a meeting stops being a mystery: what step, how long, and one click to the details."],[916,"These options are on by default in this beta and can be switched off in\nSettings. The wording when a speech-model download is paused is clearer."],[976,"This beta's supported model is Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, prepared for Apple's\nruntime."],[803,"This tester build includes evaluation-only Computer History modes; ordinary\nbuilds don't include them."],[813,"This tester build includes evaluation-only Computer History modes; ordinary\nbuilds don't include them."],[825,"This tester build includes e