[634,"To connect a provider:"],[690,"To go back to the previous search, choose &#x2A;*Apple (previous)** under **Search\nmodel** in **Settings → AI & summaries → Files you include**. Nothing is lost,\nand you can switch back at any time. With Apple chosen, the search model\ndoesn't download."],[504,"To redo one meeting, open it and choose **More → Re-analyze Audio**,\n&#x2A;*Re-analyze with the Detailed model (slower)**, or &#x2A;*Re-analyze with…** to\npick a model."],[847,"To use Nemotron for both on an existing setup, open Settings → Speech, choose\nNemotron under Transcription and press Set up. In a small test Parakeet got\nmore words right, so this beta doesn't claim Nemotron is more accurate."],[251,"To wrap up, press **Stop & Review** (⌘R). **Discard** throws the\nday away, after asking."],[456,"To-dos from a meeting"],[406,"Today and Timeline"],[239,"Today's focus"],[1153,"Today's Focus is now smarter, always visible, and reachable from every meeting."],[1149,"Today's Focus is sharper and lands in Reminders:"],[160,"Transcribe"],[181,"Transcribe any audio or video file with the on-device speech engines. The file\nis decoded to audio and recognized locally — nothing leaves your Mac."],[519,"Transcribe meetings in 25 European languages: which languages the speech model covers."],[1165,"Trust and privacy hardening:"],[300,"Turn your days into an Obsidian-style vault of linked Markdown notes or a knowledge graph in GraphML and Mermaid, and save any meeting's transcript or audio. Everything stays on your Mac."],[1223,"Turning the pages — fixed, and nicer."],[1193,"Two fixes to the Second Brain."],[1277,"Type in &#x2A;*Ask a question about your history…** and press Return\n(Shift-Return for a new line). Everpaper answers from\nwhat it has kept: your screen history and activity, up to three recorded\nmeetings, and files in folders you added under **Settings → AI & summaries →\nFiles you include**. It finds those sources by meaning, not only by matching\nwords (see Search by meaning); on macOS 27 that\nincludes what a screenshot shows and what was heard in a meeting."],[132,"Under **Start prompt**, choose when the notification arrives:"],[590,"under the switch above"],[1295,"Updates & Support"],[1300,"Updates and your meetings"],[292,"Use ←/→ to turn pages and ⌘D to jump to a\ndate. **Ask the book** (⌘F) at the top of Timeline searches across\nevery day; see Recall."],[1306,"Use the most recent link you were sent. Older links can stop working once a\nnewer build is out. To see what changed, read the\nrelease notes."],[359,"Used a Hindsight-branded build of this app before? Everpaper keeps the same\ndata, so there's nothing to import. Coming from the original Hindsight app?\n&#x2A;*Settings → General → Setup & data → Import from Hindsight (legacy)** copies\nits data into Everpaper and leaves the originals untouched."],[981,"Verified before release: notarized by Apple, signature and update-key checks passed, and the full test suite green."],[336,"Welcome"],[402,"Welcome"],[210,"What an agent reads is then handled by that app and the AI it uses, which may\nbe a cloud service. **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** doesn't apply to\nit, so turn MCP on only for apps you trust."],[696,"What changed in each version of Everpaper, newest first."],[525,"What connects to the internet"],[119,"What Everpaper keeps from your calendar"],[2,"What Everpaper uses AI for, the private models it can run on your Mac, and exactly when text leaves it."],[233,"What gets captured"],[400,"What is Everpaper: requirements, features and privacy defaults on one page."],[441,"What is Everpaper: the product facts on one page."],[471,"What it does"],[254,"What it keeps"],[1267,"What it learns about you"],[641,"What leaves your Mac: how the data path compares with other memory and meeting apps."],[6,"What setup picks"],[3,"What uses AI"],[311,"What you get:"],[650,"What you keep coming back to"],[405,"What's inside"],[774,"What's new in Everpaper, newest first. During the private beta each build\narrives as a download link and installs over the previous one; automatic\nupdates begin with the first public release. See\nUpdates & Support."],[290,"When a document stays in front for a little while, Today can show a quiet\n**RELATED TO** line naming it, with up to three related past moments, meetings\nor files. Click one to open it, or ✕ to hide them. There are no\nnotifications, and skipped apps, skipped sites and private windows never\ntrigger it. Turn it off with **Show related moments** in **Settings →\nSpeech**."],[10,"When AI work runs"],[505,"When an AI provider is set up, each finished meeting gets a **Summary** card,\nmarked *Automatic*, on its Overview tab. Everpaper writes one for meetings from\nthe last 7 days with more than a few minutes of talk (about 4,000 characters of\ntranscript), and for any older meeting when you open it. It waits about half a\nminute for speaker names and the title to settle, and never runs while you're\nrecording. Once it's there, it replaces the As we go digest. A local provider\nkeeps it on your Mac. With a cloud provider, it waits until you turn on\n**Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** in **Settings → AI & summaries**."],[870,"When reporting a wrong or flickering label, include the meeting's length, how\nmany people spoke, and whether it was Everyday or Detailed."],[342,"When you open Everpaper"],[131,"When you pick a mode other than Off, Everpaper asks for notification permission\nso reminders can appear. If notifications are turned off in System Settings,\nEverpaper shows a warning with a shortcut to fix it."],[499,"When you press **Stop recording**, Everpaper finishes transcribing on your Mac\nand saves the meeting to **Recent meetings** on the Meetings page."],[625,"When you use a private provider (Everpaper Native; Ollama, LM Studio, oMLX or\nNativ on this Mac; or an endpoint you marked trusted), Everpaper sends the\nfull, un-redacted context. It preserves real names, emails, and phone numbers\nso Memory grounds on the real thing instead of `[REDACTED:name]` placeholders.\nOn-device providers keep all of it on your Mac. A trusted endpoint receives it\nas is, which is why you should mark only a server you control. Secrets (cards,\nkeys, tokens) are still scrubbed for every provider, local or cloud."],[671,"When you want an answer rather than a destination, ask the book. On **Today**,\ntype in &#x2A;*Ask your memory…** (or choose **Go → Ask the Book**,\n⇧⌘A, to jump there), or try a chip such as &#x2A;What did I decide?*. In **Timeline**, **Ask the\nbook** (⌘F) opens the same search across every day."],[584,"Where"],[158,"Where the binary lives"],[304,"Where the files land"],[535,"Where to configure it"],[117,"Where upcoming meetings appear"],[242,"Where your data is stored"],[536,"Where your keys are stored"],[11,"Where your text goes"],[485,"Whether meetings hear the call through System Audio Recording (lighter) or through screen capture, with **Allow now** or **Check again**."],[495,"While a meeting is active, a small pill floats on top of every app."],[245,"While it runs, Everpaper keeps a private record of your workday. In the default\nmode, Screen history, it takes a screenshot of each display every 2 minutes,\nreads the text on screen so you can find anything you saw, and writes the day\nup when you stop."],[247,"While the journal runs you'll see:"],[279,"While you record a meeting, Screen history and Activity only pause on their\nown and resume when the meeting ends. Detailed screen history keeps taking its\nextra images during the meeting, with your skip rules applied. Clicks and\ntyped text stay paused in every mode. You can still mark moments. What was said in the meeting is\nincluded in that evening's entry. If you press **Stop & Review** while a\nmeeting is still recording, your day is prepared while the meeting carries on."],[642,"Who hears your meetings: where audio goes with bot-based and cloud notetakers."],[521,"Who hears your meetings: where meeting audio goes."],[152,"With a behavior other than Off, the **Upcoming** card on the Meetings page lists\nyour next matching meetings for the coming week, and lets you switch\n**When a meeting starts** (Off, Notify, Auto-start) and **Meeting eligibility**\nwithout opening Settings. The **Next meeting** card on Today shows the next one.\nClick **Record now** to start a recording named after it."],[639,"With a cloud provider, **Allow cloud AI to analyze your journal** appears under\n**Your memory & summaries**. It is off by default and is also in Privacy as\n**Allow online journal analysis**. Turn it on, and **Share your profile with\ncloud AI** appears beneath it; it sends your name, role and what you wrote\nabout yourself. With only on-device or trusted providers, the page instead\nsays &#x2A;Your AI uses only on-device or trusted private providers — cloud AI is\noff.* The MCP switches are under **Access from other AI apps**."],[378,"With Activity only and no meetings, there's nothing to grant. Granting a\npermission does not start recording. If the status doesn't update, see\nGranting Screen Recording."],[1276,"With an AI model connected, Everpaper writes a short **Reflection**: up to\nthree observations about your recent work, each marked with the captured\nmoments it comes from (\"From 3 captured moments\"). It's written at the first\nquiet moment after you open Everpaper, and after you end a day. When\nEverpaper starts at login without opening a window, it waits until you open\nit, or for a quiet moment about 15 minutes later. To see it, click the arrow beside the counts\nat the top of Memory; on the Ask tab, click the chart button (**Memory\ndetails**). A model on this Mac keeps it private: Everpaper Native (macOS 27),\noMLX, LM Studio, Ollama or Nativ. See AI on your Mac."],[515,"With an AI provider set up, **Today's focus** on the Today page picks up action\nitems from your recent meetings by itself. To pull them from one meeting\nyourself, for example after fixing the transcript, open it and choose **More →\nExtract To-Dos into Today**. Each to-do is labeled with the meeting it came\nfrom."],[99,"With Everpaper Native selected, the same place lists its models by name: set\none up (**Set up** or **Get**, followed by the model's name), **Cancel** a\ndownload, or **Remove** a model that's installed but not in use. To go through\nthe guided choice again, use **Settings → General → Setup & data → Run setup\nagain**."],[175,"Work with your saved meeting recordings and their transcripts."],[17,"Works without one"],[24,"Written answers in &#x2A;*Ask your memory…**, &#x2A;*Ask this day…**, &#x2A;*Ask this meeting…** and the **Ask** tab of Memory (also called Second Brain)"],[1263,"You"],[1274,"You can ask questions once the page reads **Getting to know you** and an AI\nmodel is connected. Until then, Ask still shows your saved conversations, and\nInsights asks you to keep journaling."],[289,"You can check a to-do off, dismiss it, or press **Add to Reminders**. Each\nto-do becomes its own reminder in a Reminders list called **Everpaper** and\nstays open in Today. The first time, macOS asks for access to Reminders.\n**View all tasks** shows the full list."],[176,"You can refer to a meeting by its full ID, a unique ID prefix (at least four hex\ncharacters), or its exact title (letter case doesn't matter)."],[390,"You land on **Today**, or on **Meetings** if you chose My meetings. Finishing\nsetup never starts a recording or a workday journal:"],[244,"You start the journal on **Today** (or **Capture → Open Day Journal**,\n⌘N), choose what it keeps in **Settings → Daily history**, and find\nfinished days in **Timeline**."],[308,"You'll find it in **Memory** (also called Second Brain) in the sidebar\n(⌘4 also opens it). Choose the **Export** tab (⌥⌘6)."],[640,"Your API key is stored only in the **macOS Keychain**, in a per-provider entry\nunder an Everpaper-specific service. It is never written to the app's\npreferences and never appears in your saved configuration. Switching providers\nkeeps each provider's key in the Keychain, so you can move back and forth without\nre-entering it. **Clear** disconnects the current AI and removes its key from\nthe Keychain. To change a key, paste the new one and press **Save**."],[827,"Your daily journal reads like a diary again, meetings get a summary, and\nGemma 4 joins the local models."],[125,"Your events stay on your Mac, and Everpaper never uploads them. Everpaper keeps\nno copy of your calendar."],[241,"Your finished days (Timeline)"],[632,"Your journal and meetings are stored in Everpaper's folder in your user\nLibrary. Some downloaded models are kept elsewhere, so remove models with the\nbuttons above rather than by deleting folders."],[4,"Your options"],[41,"your own app on this Mac"],[295,"Your screenshots, text, timeline, entries and notes are stored on this Mac, in\nEverpaper's folder in your user Library. To keep a copy elsewhere, use\nExport."],[1159,"Your Second Brain now genuinely thinks about your work — and the whole app got sharper, more honest, and more consistent."],[1144,"Your Second Brain now leads with genuine AI insight, reads your own files, and works reliably on local models — all on-device, all private."],[1196,"Your Second Brain now understands *you* — not just the people, files, and projects in\nyour work, but who you are and how your days have been going."],[324,"Your word list can be saved too: in Settings → **Speech** → **Your words &\nphrases**, **Backup** has &#x2A;*Export…**."]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":41,"2":42,"3":43,"4":44,"5":45,"6":46,"7":47,"8":48,"9":49,"10":50,"11":51,"12":52,"13":53,"14":54,"15":55,"16":56,"17":57,"18":58,"19":59,"20":60,"21":61,"22":62,"23":63,"24":64,"25":65,"26":66,"27":67,"28":68,"29":69,"30":70,"31":71,"32":72,"33":73,"34":74,"35":75,"36":76,"37":77,"38":78,"39":79,"40":80,"41":81,"42":82,"43":83,"44":84,"45":85,"46":86,"47":87,"48":88,"49":89,"